1
00:02:11,720 --> 00:02:14,640
﻿We thought you were a veteran warrior.

2
00:02:18,520 --> 00:02:20,560
﻿But it seems..

3
00:02:21,720 --> 00:02:25,840
...you are now going on
campaigns with raiders.

4
00:02:31,160 --> 00:02:34,240
﻿It doesn't suit you, Osman Bey.

5
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:39,560
﻿Were you going to take Lefke like this?

6
00:02:39,600 --> 00:02:42,080
﻿If we are so worthless,

7
00:02:42,240 --> 00:02:45,920
﻿-Why did he send his son...
-We fight for Islam!

8
00:02:49,320 --> 00:02:53,160
﻿It doesn't matter with whom or what for.

9
00:02:53,320 --> 00:02:55,800
﻿We always intend to conquer!

10
00:02:55,840 --> 00:02:59,920
﻿I like this upright stand of yours.

11
00:03:00,320 --> 00:03:02,520
﻿You are a brave man.

12
00:03:02,720 --> 00:03:07,600
﻿But it doesn't suit you, Osman Bey.

13
00:03:15,120 --> 00:03:18,120
﻿-Come on!
-Lefke Castle..

14
00:03:18,200 --> 00:03:21,120
﻿..is your property now!

15
00:03:34,160 --> 00:03:36,840
﻿Settle in with your alps.

16
00:03:37,200 --> 00:03:40,680
﻿May your reputation spread among Turkmen!

17
00:03:40,960 --> 00:03:46,080
﻿May many brave warriors stand beside you!

18
00:03:58,760 --> 00:04:02,800
﻿What are you saying, Yakup Bey?

19
00:04:08,200 --> 00:04:10,640
﻿This place is your sword right.

20
00:04:11,720 --> 00:04:14,480
﻿You took it by fighting.

21
00:04:16,800 --> 00:04:21,160
﻿Why would it be my property? Why?

22
00:04:23,280 --> 00:04:28,640
﻿Because you are the one who fights most.

23
00:04:31,520 --> 00:04:36,920
﻿Lefke is our closest border to Byzantine.

24
00:04:37,320 --> 00:04:41,120
﻿It will be headquarters for conquests.

25
00:05:05,160 --> 00:05:08,320
﻿For this reason, Lefke..

26
00:05:08,680 --> 00:05:14,720
...should belong to Osman Bey who has been
fighting from father to son.

27
00:05:20,720 --> 00:05:23,360
Thank you.

28
00:05:25,560 --> 00:05:27,440
Thank you.

29
00:05:27,680 --> 00:05:32,200
﻿Do you doubt the firman?

30
00:05:33,800 --> 00:05:37,880
﻿No. You took Lefke.

31
00:05:38,520 --> 00:05:44,080
You conquered this place.
You left me nothing to doubt.

32
00:05:44,560 --> 00:05:47,600
﻿This is what you were expected to do, anyway.

33
00:05:47,760 --> 00:05:52,400
﻿We expect some things from you too, Osman Bey.

34
00:05:53,240 --> 00:05:56,600
﻿When will you pledge loyalty?

35
00:06:04,840 --> 00:06:07,440
﻿Yakup Bey.

36
00:06:10,080 --> 00:06:13,760
When the Messenger of the Worlds
(PBUH) passed away,

37
00:06:14,080 --> 00:06:16,680
﻿...even Hadhrat Ali (RA)...

38
00:06:17,120 --> 00:06:21,320
...didn't pledge loyalty for
Hadhrat Abu Bakr(RA) instantly.

39
00:06:25,160 --> 00:06:27,760
﻿Don't push me.

40
00:06:28,600 --> 00:06:31,480
﻿Don't push me.

41
00:06:35,760 --> 00:06:38,840
﻿Besides, a quick oath of loyalty...

42
00:06:39,760 --> 00:06:42,480
﻿..would be no good.

43
00:06:44,560 --> 00:06:48,320
﻿You are right, but...

44
00:06:48,400 --> 00:06:54,240
We should be united these days.
These are the last days of humanity.

45
00:06:55,040 --> 00:06:57,520
﻿You should be quick.

46
00:07:01,560 --> 00:07:06,400
﻿Cerkutay Bey has found the right way.

47
00:07:07,560 --> 00:07:10,720
﻿He's under my command.

48
00:07:12,600 --> 00:07:17,880
﻿He's the patron of the frontier market now.

49
00:07:24,960 --> 00:07:27,480
﻿What?

50
00:07:27,480 --> 00:07:30,920
﻿I guess you don't like this, Osman Bey.

51
00:07:32,160 --> 00:07:34,720
﻿Quite the contrary.

52
00:07:38,200 --> 00:07:43,840
Well... Instead of walking around aimlessly,
he should be with Yakup Bey.

53
00:07:44,480 --> 00:07:46,880
﻿So he will do his duties properly.

54
00:07:52,720 --> 00:07:58,440
Tomorrow, come to the frontier
market with your family.

55
00:07:59,360 --> 00:08:03,640
﻿We shall eat and talk about conquests.

56
00:08:03,720 --> 00:08:06,560
﻿And about loyalty.

57
00:08:08,280 --> 00:08:14,080
﻿This matter should come to a conclusion.

58
00:08:21,600 --> 00:08:25,400
﻿I will come to talk about conquests.

59
00:08:43,280 --> 00:08:48,880
Your upright head will either
bow or leave your shoulders, Osman.

60
00:08:49,280 --> 00:08:53,160
﻿He doesn't intend to make me bow, but crush me.

61
00:08:53,280 --> 00:08:57,640
﻿Make whatever game you want. I will ruin your games.

62
00:08:59,600 --> 00:09:02,960
﻿Orhan, stop.

63
00:09:04,360 --> 00:09:07,240
﻿You're wounded so you need to rest.

64
00:09:07,360 --> 00:09:10,080
﻿This isn't a good time for resting, Holofira.

65
00:09:10,280 --> 00:09:16,240
Crusaders must have hit the road
to take the gold to their lands.

66
00:09:16,520 --> 00:09:19,240
﻿I need to catch them and take the gold.

67
00:09:19,440 --> 00:09:22,720
﻿Otherwise I will never be able to take it.

68
00:09:23,200 --> 00:09:27,640
﻿But you're not coming. You will go to a safe place.

69
00:09:28,120 --> 00:09:30,440
﻿No.

70
00:09:35,280 --> 00:09:39,840
-I can't leave you like this.
-Holofira.

71
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:43,880
﻿I need to catch the crusaders. Let me go.

72
00:09:44,040 --> 00:09:48,120
﻿How do you know they are crusaders?

73
00:09:53,880 --> 00:09:57,360
﻿They were wearing crusader clothes, Dervish.

74
00:09:58,480 --> 00:10:01,040
﻿Is this your proof?

75
00:10:04,600 --> 00:10:10,240
You only saw their clothes.
Do you know their hearts?

76
00:10:11,800 --> 00:10:16,640
﻿Let's say we made this tree wear clothes.

77
00:10:17,120 --> 00:10:19,920
﻿Would it become a human?

78
00:10:25,040 --> 00:10:30,240
﻿You say the attackers weren't crusaders?

79
00:10:30,680 --> 00:10:33,520
﻿I don't know that.

80
00:10:38,200 --> 00:10:41,720
﻿-Karaali.
-My Shahzade.

81
00:10:42,360 --> 00:10:45,720
﻿Now go and bring what I want.

82
00:10:45,760 --> 00:10:48,320
﻿Listen to me well.

83
00:10:55,040 --> 00:10:58,200
﻿-Come on.
-As you order, my Shahzade.

84
00:11:01,840 --> 00:11:07,040
﻿Thank you for healing me, Dervish.

85
00:11:07,160 --> 00:11:11,960
﻿Now I should get going.

86
00:11:12,240 --> 00:11:14,680
﻿Allah is the Healer.

87
00:11:14,840 --> 00:11:17,960
-Stay safe.
-Thank you.

88
00:11:31,360 --> 00:11:37,080
﻿My Bey, why did Yakup Bey hand over Lefke?

89
00:11:37,240 --> 00:11:39,920
﻿He is showing power, brother.

90
00:11:40,040 --> 00:11:43,920
He wants to seem generous
and strengthen his position.

91
00:11:45,520 --> 00:11:50,280
Pardon my curiosity, my Bey.
But why did you accept it?

92
00:11:51,920 --> 00:11:56,240
﻿Yakup Bey has never been honest to us.

93
00:11:57,080 --> 00:12:02,720
He's making such a game that
if you don't act cautiously...

94
00:12:02,960 --> 00:12:05,560
﻿...you can find yourself in chains.

95
00:12:07,440 --> 00:12:13,400
He handed over the castle but he thought
I wouldn't take the castle.

96
00:12:13,600 --> 00:12:18,240
If I hadn't taken it,
he would have convinced the beys.

97
00:12:18,600 --> 00:12:22,680
He would have said "I gave him a castle.
He didn't even take it."

98
00:12:22,840 --> 00:12:28,480
He doesn't want to fight for Islam.
He's arrogant and has a problem with me."

99
00:12:28,800 --> 00:12:33,760
﻿He would have said "Osman Bey is our enemy".

100
00:12:34,920 --> 00:12:39,560
﻿"He doesn't even mind firman or conquest."

101
00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:44,000
﻿Is the firman real, Osman Bey?

102
00:12:44,080 --> 00:12:46,320
﻿The seal is real.

103
00:12:46,600 --> 00:12:49,520
﻿But the firma

104
00:12:50,760 --> 00:12:54,880
Sultan gave the treasure to us.
Why would he give him the firman?

105
00:12:54,960 --> 00:12:58,160
﻿There must be a trick about it.

106
00:12:58,360 --> 00:13:03,760
﻿Taking even Cerkutay on his side is a part of his game.

107
00:13:04,080 --> 00:13:08,400
He does it to be able to say
"Even his own men come to me".

108
00:13:09,080 --> 00:13:11,240
﻿He attacks from all directions.

109
00:13:11,240 --> 00:13:13,880
﻿You're right, Bala.

110
00:13:14,080 --> 00:13:17,320
He isn't like any enemies
who we have fought so far.

111
00:13:17,480 --> 00:13:21,600
﻿So we should be careful.

112
00:13:23,440 --> 00:13:25,960
﻿'ueuiso

113
00:13:26,720 --> 00:13:30,240
﻿Why did you let Cerkutay go?

114
00:13:31,840 --> 00:13:35,840
If you had held him here,
he might have understood.

115
00:13:38,240 --> 00:13:43,680
﻿Bala, sometimes a sentence...

116
00:13:44,400 --> 00:13:47,280
﻿...says a thousand.

117
00:13:50,280 --> 00:13:52,880
﻿You know what he said to me?

118
00:13:53,200 --> 00:13:55,240
﻿"Osman Bey,

119
00:13:55,520 --> 00:13:58,960
...I remained a prisoner
for years for your cause."

120
00:13:58,960 --> 00:14:02,640
﻿Now tell me. Tell me!

121
00:14:02,720 --> 00:14:05,480
﻿Is this Osman Bey's cause?

122
00:14:07,760 --> 00:14:13,040
This is the cause of Allah.
This is the cause of our Prophet (PBUH).

123
00:14:15,960 --> 00:14:20,120
﻿We serve this cause. Don't we, Boran?

124
00:14:20,200 --> 00:14:22,480
﻿Konur? Tell me.

125
00:14:22,760 --> 00:14:26,200
-This is the cause of Allah.
-There is no self.

126
00:14:27,480 --> 00:14:32,600
﻿We serve Him. That's why I let him go.

127
00:14:32,680 --> 00:14:37,760
Well, there is nothing to do but praying
for him to come back to the path of Allah.

128
00:14:38,160 --> 00:14:42,720
﻿But there is something to do about Yakup Bey.

129
00:14:43,160 --> 00:14:46,000
﻿Quickly as well.

130
00:14:47,840 --> 00:14:50,240
﻿Konur.

131
00:14:50,520 --> 00:14:54,560
You will keep order at the castle.
Do not leave the Bannerless alone.

132
00:14:54,640 --> 00:14:56,040
﻿As you command, Bey.

133
00:14:56,120 --> 00:14:57,200
﻿-Bora.
-Bey.

134
00:14:57,280 --> 00:14:59,720
﻿Look at each secret passage.

135
00:14:59,800 --> 00:15:03,000
﻿Count the warehouse after counting the spoils.

136
00:15:03,080 --> 00:15:04,880
﻿As you command.

137
00:15:06,080 --> 00:15:09,480
﻿Tell Alaeddin to not leave Yakup Bey alone.

138
00:15:09,760 --> 00:15:12,560
﻿-As you command, Bey.
-Quickly.

139
00:15:15,720 --> 00:15:17,720
﻿My Bala.

140
00:15:18,240 --> 00:15:22,280
﻿-Come on.
-I can not come to Yenisehir, Osman.

141
00:15:22,920 --> 00:15:28,480
Bala, what are you saying?
You are better than before now.

142
00:15:28,560 --> 00:15:32,560
﻿-No, Osman.
-Bala.

143
00:15:32,800 --> 00:15:39,120
Sogut is entrusted to me,
as the state is entrusted to you.

144
00:15:39,240 --> 00:15:44,520
And my father is not here.
You are on a difficult path, Osman.

145
00:15:44,600 --> 00:15:48,680
You need people beside you.
The guild, sisters..

146
00:15:48,760 --> 00:15:51,360
﻿I need to take care of them.

147
00:15:51,480 --> 00:15:56,760
﻿Here is where people grow.

148
00:15:58,800 --> 00:16:02,760
﻿My Bala, I understand you well.

149
00:16:03,360 --> 00:16:06,520
﻿After all the sacrifice you made..

150
00:16:06,600 --> 00:16:10,480
Will lead us to victory
against the enemy, however..

151
00:16:10,840 --> 00:16:13,440
﻿Bala.

152
00:16:27,840 --> 00:16:32,240
﻿The tracks of carts and horses.

153
00:16:36,880 --> 00:16:40,000
﻿Is more visible here.

154
00:16:41,560 --> 00:16:44,160
﻿These are theirs.

155
00:16:48,360 --> 00:16:50,280
﻿Let us go after them at once.

156
00:16:50,360 --> 00:16:54,960
﻿Orhan. I know, your blood boils.

157
00:16:55,040 --> 00:16:58,200
However, I don't want you to do something
unwise when you find them.

158
00:16:58,280 --> 00:17:02,840
﻿Those gold coins, is the future of my nation.

159
00:17:02,920 --> 00:17:04,880
﻿And my task is clear.

160
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:09,680
﻿I will do everything I can to get that treasure.

161
00:17:09,760 --> 00:17:11,960
﻿Even if it costs your life?

162
00:17:13,920 --> 00:17:16,599
﻿Even if it costs my life.

163
00:17:26,680 --> 00:17:30,000
﻿Burn them in the cave.

164
00:17:37,720 --> 00:17:41,160
﻿We've got double the spoils in one raid..

165
00:17:41,240 --> 00:17:44,720
Compared to pillaging,
all thanks to you Mehmet Bey.

166
00:17:44,800 --> 00:17:49,760
﻿Doing business with you is profitable.

167
00:17:50,120 --> 00:17:55,280
Yes, Atmaca.
This is the power of Germiyanoglu.

168
00:17:56,280 --> 00:17:59,040
﻿Those who serve..

169
00:17:59,520 --> 00:18:03,240
﻿Fill their sacks with plenty of gold like this.

170
00:18:03,360 --> 00:18:06,560
We will do more business with you
in the future, Mehmet Bey.

171
00:18:06,640 --> 00:18:10,560
Those who wish to bring these
gold coins to the frontier bazaar..

172
00:18:10,960 --> 00:18:15,280
﻿And want to reach our power will fail.

173
00:18:15,440 --> 00:18:20,440
﻿My Shahzade. Caravan is ready to depart.

174
00:18:26,800 --> 00:18:31,600
Quickly then, we will take
no breaks until frontier bazaar.

175
00:18:32,800 --> 00:18:37,960
﻿-Gonca Hatun.
-Hear what you're saying.

176
00:18:38,400 --> 00:18:40,840
﻿-Baysungur.
-My Shahzade.

177
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:44,000
﻿Sheathe your swords and stay back.

178
00:18:44,320 --> 00:18:46,880
Gulce.

179
00:18:57,600 --> 00:19:02,280
-Were you scared?
-You know that I did not.

180
00:19:02,360 --> 00:19:05,560
I have no business with
your father as well, Trickster Hatun.

181
00:19:05,640 --> 00:19:08,040
﻿I was very bored at the bazaar.

182
00:19:08,160 --> 00:19:11,240
﻿And since no one is racing horses.

183
00:19:11,480 --> 00:19:16,480
Then I said,
"If I go out of this bazaar now.."

184
00:19:16,720 --> 00:19:19,480
﻿"Who would follow me?"

185
00:19:19,560 --> 00:19:23,080
﻿-Of course the Trickster Hatun.
-Allah Allah.

186
00:19:23,160 --> 00:19:26,320
﻿You did all this confusion for horse racing?

187
00:19:26,440 --> 00:19:29,240
﻿Don't you think it was worth it?

188
00:19:30,560 --> 00:19:35,880
We could not do it last time.
Maybe this time I will beat you.

189
00:19:35,960 --> 00:19:39,920
﻿However, no trickery.

190
00:19:42,320 --> 00:19:47,080
﻿If I win, you will not call me trickster anymore.

191
00:19:47,160 --> 00:19:50,800
﻿Alright. What if I win?

192
00:19:50,880 --> 00:19:53,200
﻿You won't.

193
00:19:53,280 --> 00:19:57,040
Let's say you did,
what do you want?

194
00:19:58,080 --> 00:20:01,960
﻿You can find out after Trickster Hatun.

195
00:20:02,040 --> 00:20:03,640
﻿Alright.

196
00:20:04,040 --> 00:20:06,960
﻿-To the bazaar then.
-Alright.

197
00:20:07,040 --> 00:20:09,120
﻿As you say, Trickster Hatun.

198
00:20:09,200 --> 00:20:12,680
This was the last time
you called me Trickster Hatun.

199
00:20:15,160 --> 00:20:17,720
﻿We will see.

200
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:21,360
﻿Quickly.

201
00:20:24,440 --> 00:20:27,320
﻿Quickly.

202
00:20:30,520 --> 00:20:34,040
﻿-Quickly!
-Quickly!

203
00:20:46,640 --> 00:20:49,520
﻿Come on!

204
00:20:51,240 --> 00:20:54,040
﻿Quickly!

205
00:21:11,640 --> 00:21:14,520
﻿Come on!

206
00:21:19,600 --> 00:21:22,320
My Bey, public order was
maintained at castle.

207
00:21:22,320 --> 00:21:26,560
The secret passages are being searched,
we are putting up guards.

208
00:21:26,640 --> 00:21:29,480
Yakup Bey and his men
did not touch the treasure, Bey.

209
00:21:29,720 --> 00:21:32,240
﻿All of it is there.

210
00:21:32,320 --> 00:21:34,920
Alright.

211
00:21:40,440 --> 00:21:45,640
﻿-Quickly.
-May your conquest be glorious, Osman Bey.

212
00:21:46,600 --> 00:21:51,080
You are a providential man.
You got the castle without shedding blood.

213
00:21:51,160 --> 00:21:54,680
-Praise be!
-You are providential as well.

214
00:21:56,000 --> 00:21:59,520
You got spoils without
drawing your swords.

215
00:22:03,680 --> 00:22:07,760
However Osman Bey,
you told us there were no treasure.

216
00:22:07,920 --> 00:22:10,320
And we said it's alright.

217
00:22:10,600 --> 00:22:12,720
﻿No.

218
00:22:13,360 --> 00:22:16,360
﻿-We do not want it.
-What's that?

219
00:22:16,520 --> 00:22:19,640
﻿Are you disobeying my command?

220
00:22:23,040 --> 00:22:29,040
-No, Osman Bey.
-It is most propitious to give to the ones that does not want it.

221
00:22:32,280 --> 00:22:34,480
﻿-Bora.
-Bey.

222
00:22:34,600 --> 00:22:37,320
Distribute the Banerless' treasure.

223
00:22:37,440 --> 00:22:39,880
﻿As you command.

224
00:22:41,960 --> 00:22:44,160
﻿Konur.

225
00:22:44,600 --> 00:22:48,040
And you maintain order of the castle
and come back to Yenisehir.

226
00:22:48,120 --> 00:22:50,640
﻿-As you command Bey.
-Come on.

227
00:22:50,800 --> 00:22:53,760
﻿Bannerless, quickly.

228
00:22:53,920 --> 00:22:56,520
﻿Osman Bey.

229
00:22:59,040 --> 00:23:02,640
﻿Do not call us "Bannerless" anymore.

230
00:23:09,920 --> 00:23:15,120
﻿We are fighting under the Banner of Kayi now.

231
00:23:19,400 --> 00:23:20,600
Good.

232
00:23:23,200 --> 00:23:24,520
﻿Quickly.

233
00:24:09,800 --> 00:24:15,840
﻿Mehmet... So you were behind this, huh?

234
00:24:18,840 --> 00:24:23,960
﻿Isn't that him? From the Bannerless...

235
00:24:24,040 --> 00:24:28,200
﻿I swear... I won't let you have that...

236
00:24:28,320 --> 00:24:31,080
﻿...treasure you took with treachery.

237
00:24:36,440 --> 00:24:41,600
My Shahzade.
We brought the Mongol clothes you wanted.

238
00:24:43,240 --> 00:24:47,920
﻿Good. Wear the clothes and paint your face.

239
00:24:48,120 --> 00:24:51,640
﻿We will raid their place.

240
00:24:53,500 --> 00:24:56,950
How are you going to fight against
all those men with 6 people, Orhan?

241
00:24:56,950 --> 00:24:58,310
Are you out of your mind?

242
00:24:58,310 --> 00:25:03,120
Do not mind their number, Holofira.
Once, my ancestor Kursad...

243
00:25:03,240 --> 00:25:09,560
...defeated everyone in a palace with his 40 valiants.
And now, with my 6 valiants...

244
00:25:09,880 --> 00:25:12,920
﻿..I will ruin them.

245
00:25:13,880 --> 00:25:18,720
When I take the gold with my valiants,
I will prove myself...

246
00:25:18,840 --> 00:25:22,040
...and gain my father's trust

247
00:25:25,360 --> 00:25:28,880
﻿Okay then. I will fight with you.

248
00:25:29,040 --> 00:25:30,480
﻿No.

249
00:25:31,480 --> 00:25:35,640
﻿You will not come.
You will stand back.

250
00:25:38,640 --> 00:25:41,160
﻿Alps.

251
00:25:42,720 --> 00:25:46,440
﻿Now listen to me carefully.

252
00:25:46,440 --> 00:25:47,720
GERMIYANOGULLARI BORDER

253
00:26:03,160 --> 00:26:05,400
﻿Malhun Hatun.

254
00:26:08,560 --> 00:26:11,720
﻿Ulgen Hatun is also here.

255
00:26:16,600 --> 00:26:20,720
Won't you feel a little upset
when you are stepping on...

256
00:26:20,800 --> 00:26:24,080
﻿...that carpet with your muddy feet, Ulgen?

257
00:26:24,160 --> 00:26:27,040
﻿I didn't know what to do.

258
00:26:29,240 --> 00:26:33,600
﻿I am trying to be silent and keep it in...

259
00:26:33,680 --> 00:26:37,480
...Cerkutay does not know
what he is doing, but what about you?

260
00:26:37,560 --> 00:26:42,840
Couldn't you inform me, Ulgen?
What does working in the marketplace mean?

261
00:26:43,040 --> 00:26:46,640
Don't you know what's going to
happen when Osman Bey hears this?

262
00:26:46,720 --> 00:26:51,080
﻿How can't you resist Cerkutay?

263
00:26:51,160 --> 00:26:54,240
﻿I couldn't stop him no matter what I did.

264
00:26:54,800 --> 00:26:56,440
﻿Forgive me.

265
00:26:58,720 --> 00:27:04,240
I thought you were my sister,
but what you did did not suit you, Ulgen Hatun.

266
00:27:04,360 --> 00:27:09,600
﻿You are now standing next to our enemy, not us.

267
00:27:09,680 --> 00:27:12,880
﻿I would never expect this from you.

268
00:27:33,280 --> 00:27:37,840
﻿Alps visited villages and tribes around Yenisehir.

269
00:27:37,920 --> 00:27:42,120
﻿They took all the carpets on the counters.

270
00:27:42,520 --> 00:27:46,880
﻿They will give them in the morning tomorrow.

271
00:27:49,120 --> 00:27:53,040
﻿Once Malhun Hatun's caravan is raided...

272
00:27:53,120 --> 00:27:56,040
﻿...and when she can't find goods to buy...

273
00:27:56,120 --> 00:27:59,640
...let's see what she will
sell with an empty counter.

274
00:28:07,000 --> 00:28:10,400
﻿It is high time you approached Ulgen.

275
00:28:11,000 --> 00:28:14,480
﻿Be around her.

276
00:28:26,520 --> 00:28:29,440
﻿Mother... Saadet Hatun..

277
00:28:29,560 --> 00:28:34,320
...wanted to buy all the carpets
in the villages and tribes around Yenisehir.

278
00:28:35,800 --> 00:28:39,480
﻿Hatuns sent news to ask what to do.

279
00:28:40,160 --> 00:28:42,640
﻿Saadet..

280
00:28:43,640 --> 00:28:46,880
﻿You want to play a game against me, huh?

281
00:28:47,040 --> 00:28:49,120
﻿When will they buy the carpets?

282
00:28:49,120 --> 00:28:52,720
They said they would give those carpets
tomorrow morning to Alps to gain some time.

283
00:28:52,720 --> 00:28:55,480
﻿They are waiting for your order, mother.

284
00:28:58,000 --> 00:29:01,000
﻿I will play such a game against Saadet that...

285
00:29:01,080 --> 00:29:04,320
﻿...she won't even be able to understand.

286
00:29:04,960 --> 00:29:08,080
﻿We will send news to the Hatuns right away.

287
00:29:08,160 --> 00:29:11,720
﻿Now listen to me carefully.

288
00:30:03,560 --> 00:30:07,000
﻿Oguz Alp. Come on!

289
00:30:08,000 --> 00:30:10,880
O Eternal!

290
00:30:11,160 --> 00:30:14,360
﻿Raid!

291
00:30:35,360 --> 00:30:37,600
﻿Come on!

292
00:30:42,520 --> 00:30:46,480
﻿Stay together!

293
00:30:47,400 --> 00:30:50,760
Where are they?
Where are they?

294
00:30:52,160 --> 00:30:55,240
O Eternal!

295
00:31:01,600 --> 00:31:04,440
﻿Protect the gold!

296
00:31:07,600 --> 00:31:10,560
﻿Protect the Shahzade!

297
00:31:10,960 --> 00:31:14,400
O Eternal!

298
00:31:56,080 --> 00:32:01,040
-Let's step back, Mehmed Bey.
-I won't leave the gold.

299
00:32:07,040 --> 00:32:10,160
O Eternal!

300
00:32:14,360 --> 00:32:17,600
O Eternal!

301
00:32:27,440 --> 00:32:30,440
O Eternal!

302
00:32:32,760 --> 00:32:36,520
﻿Alps! Come on!

303
00:33:28,040 --> 00:33:32,000
﻿Who are you? Who are you?

304
00:33:44,800 --> 00:33:48,560
﻿We are stepping back! Come on!

305
00:34:13,239 --> 00:34:15,920
﻿Come on!

306
00:34:20,440 --> 00:34:25,280
﻿My Shahzade... My Shahzade...

307
00:34:51,920 --> 00:34:52,840
﻿Turahan!

308
00:34:53,560 --> 00:34:56,960
Do you recognize the clothes of
the ones next to that caravan?

309
00:34:57,040 --> 00:35:01,280
They wear our clothes,
but I don't know them, my Bey.

310
00:35:07,520 --> 00:35:09,560
﻿Osman Bey...

311
00:35:09,640 --> 00:35:13,320
By the look of that caravan,
he is a wealthy trader.

312
00:35:13,400 --> 00:35:16,240
e would know him if he was from here.

313
00:35:16,680 --> 00:35:21,480
﻿We'll see. We'll see now.

314
00:35:31,640 --> 00:35:33,040
Peace be upon you.

315
00:35:33,120 --> 00:35:37,680
With Allah's mercy and grace,
peace be upon you too,

316
00:35:37,960 --> 00:35:43,720
-So you want to gain more good deeds, huh?
-Not at all, Osman Bey.

317
00:35:44,440 --> 00:35:48,320
﻿The Ummah is praying for you.

318
00:35:48,440 --> 00:35:51,320
﻿Our good deeds are nothing compared to yours.

319
00:35:51,400 --> 00:35:56,040
﻿You know us, you know what we look like.

320
00:35:57,600 --> 00:36:02,600
﻿But we don't know you. Tell me, who are you?

321
00:36:02,760 --> 00:36:06,720
﻿Where are you coming from?
Where are you going? Tell us.

322
00:36:11,160 --> 00:36:13,680
﻿Alps!

323
00:36:15,720 --> 00:36:19,360
﻿Bala, stand back. Stand back.

324
00:36:21,600 --> 00:36:25,480
﻿My Allah... My Allah, do not kill me today!

325
00:36:25,800 --> 00:36:30,640
﻿Alps! Alps! To the goods! Protect the goods!

326
00:36:30,720 --> 00:36:35,200
﻿Alps! The Bannerless! Come on!

327
00:37:28,000 --> 00:37:30,760
﻿We are even again, huh, Trickster Hatun?

328
00:37:30,800 --> 00:37:33,680
﻿I will defeat you next time, Scholar.

329
00:37:33,760 --> 00:37:36,200
﻿That's what you said earlier.

330
00:37:47,160 --> 00:37:50,880
﻿Look at you.. You are even again, huh?

331
00:37:51,000 --> 00:37:54,520
﻿Walk, Fatma. I couldn't follow Yakup Bey.

332
00:37:55,080 --> 00:37:58,520
Good, but, I won't forget these...
We'll talk about it, know that brother.

333
00:37:58,600 --> 00:38:00,960
﻿Good, come on.

334
00:38:04,240 --> 00:38:08,200
﻿My son... Are you alright?

335
00:38:08,320 --> 00:38:12,720
I am alright, mother.
But I lost track of Yakup Bey.

336
00:38:24,320 --> 00:38:30,320
Malhun Hatun, my Shahzade.
We received news from Osman Bey.

337
00:38:30,560 --> 00:38:33,040
﻿Yakup Bey...

338
00:38:33,200 --> 00:38:37,400
﻿...conquered Lefke Castle and gave it to Osman Bey.

339
00:38:40,080 --> 00:38:43,800
﻿What is that man trying to do?
-My Shahzade...

340
00:38:43,920 --> 00:38:46,880
﻿He said you will keep following Yakup Bey.

341
00:38:46,920 --> 00:38:51,320
This time we won't make a mistake.
Tell the Alps to go everywhere in the marketplace.

342
00:38:51,440 --> 00:38:54,080
﻿Everyone will be on alert.

343
00:38:54,480 --> 00:38:59,640
Alaeddin. My son...
Then you will stay here tonight.

344
00:38:59,720 --> 00:39:02,480
﻿The carpet caravan is entrusted to you.

345
00:39:02,600 --> 00:39:06,280
﻿I think Saadet will raid the caravan...

346
00:39:06,360 --> 00:39:08,760
﻿...therefore, change your route.

347
00:39:09,120 --> 00:39:12,120
﻿Yes Malhun Ha tun.

348
00:39:12,640 --> 00:39:17,480
Don't worry, Malhun mother.
I will send the Alps and take precaution.

349
00:39:20,520 --> 00:39:23,840
Have you heard, brother?
Germiyan's son Yakup Bey...

350
00:39:23,920 --> 00:39:28,160
...conquered Lefke Castle.
And he gave the castle to Osman Bey.

351
00:39:28,360 --> 00:39:32,520
﻿Yakup Bey really is an honorable man.

352
00:39:44,880 --> 00:39:49,000
-Are you alright?
-Thank Allah, I am.

353
00:39:52,120 --> 00:39:56,680
﻿There's no need. There's no need at all.

354
00:39:58,400 --> 00:40:04,960
Those crusaders are everywhere.
They cornered us, Osman Bey.

355
00:40:05,040 --> 00:40:10,120
Thankfully we came across you
otherwise we would have been ruined.

356
00:40:10,200 --> 00:40:12,680
-Thank you.
-No problem, no problem.

357
00:40:12,800 --> 00:40:18,000
We wouldn't let infidels hurt you, of course.
Tell me now.

358
00:40:18,080 --> 00:40:20,840
﻿Who are you?

359
00:40:21,200 --> 00:40:29,440
My Creator bestowed
upon us the profession of...

360
00:40:29,560 --> 00:40:34,160
﻿our Prophet (PBUH) and his companions.

361
00:40:34,280 --> 00:40:38,320
﻿As you can see, I'm a trader.

362
00:40:38,520 --> 00:40:42,680
﻿-They call me Ayhan agha.
-Ayhan agha, is that so?

363
00:40:42,800 --> 00:40:46,920
﻿-What do you have in your caravan?
-All sorts of things.

364
00:40:47,000 --> 00:40:50,080
﻿My Osman Bey, now,

365
00:40:50,160 --> 00:40:53,320
I don't want to boast myself, but...

366
00:40:53,400 --> 00:40:56,640
...I have such goods that

367
00:40:56,800 --> 00:41:00,880
﻿no one else has. I make trade with

368
00:41:01,000 --> 00:41:03,280
﻿traders from every nation.

369
00:41:12,200 --> 00:41:16,840
﻿My Osman Bey, this is our gift.

370
00:41:25,800 --> 00:41:31,800
It is the most precious piece of my caravan.
It's not enough to pay for my life debt

371
00:41:31,880 --> 00:41:36,320
﻿but we would be glad if you accept.

372
00:41:39,320 --> 00:41:41,720
﻿Osman Bey.

373
00:41:42,280 --> 00:41:48,360
﻿It is our gift, we would be sad if you turn it down.

374
00:41:48,600 --> 00:41:51,600
Thank you. Thank you.

375
00:41:51,800 --> 00:41:55,080
﻿Turahan, give it to me.

376
00:41:56,680 --> 00:42:00,000
﻿Take this in return.

377
00:42:00,200 --> 00:42:02,800
﻿No, take it.

378
00:42:02,880 --> 00:42:06,640
﻿We compensate everything we take.

379
00:42:14,240 --> 00:42:17,520
﻿Tell me, where are you headed at?

380
00:42:17,600 --> 00:42:21,400
﻿Osman Bey, I made my trade in Constantinople.

381
00:42:21,480 --> 00:42:24,120
﻿I'm going towards Karaman, but

382
00:42:24,320 --> 00:42:31,040
I hope these infidels will not stop us again.
We were planning on going to the frontier marketplace.

383
00:42:31,160 --> 00:42:33,880
﻿Frontier marketplace?

384
00:42:34,240 --> 00:42:38,480
﻿-Do you know Yakup Bey?
-Yakup Bey? No.

385
00:42:38,560 --> 00:42:44,120
I don't know him but I heard a lot
about the frontier marketplace.

386
00:42:44,280 --> 00:42:48,400
﻿It would be bad to not visit, but

387
00:42:48,560 --> 00:42:52,960
﻿I don't even want to go to a caravanserai anymore.

388
00:42:53,080 --> 00:42:56,200
﻿These dastards might attack again.

389
00:42:58,240 --> 00:43:02,200
﻿Ayhan agha, Ayhan agha we are very afraid!

390
00:43:02,360 --> 00:43:06,400
﻿Do not be afraid, do not be afraid!

391
00:43:11,240 --> 00:43:13,720
﻿Son of alps.

392
00:43:13,800 --> 00:43:19,840
We brought them with us to teach them
trading but we cannot protect their lives.

393
00:43:20,720 --> 00:43:23,600
﻿That's not right.

394
00:43:26,840 --> 00:43:29,400
﻿Sons.

395
00:43:36,600 --> 00:43:41,080
Move your caravan towards Yenisehir,
it is safer there.

396
00:43:41,200 --> 00:43:46,600
Tomorrow come to my palace, we'll go to
the marketplace as well, you can join us.

397
00:43:46,760 --> 00:43:49,120
﻿May Allah bless you Osman Bey.

398
00:43:49,240 --> 00:43:52,280
﻿We'll surely come.

399
00:43:52,960 --> 00:43:58,360
﻿Sons, there's no need. Thank you.

400
00:43:58,480 --> 00:44:02,480
May Allah bless you Osman Bey.
We will surely come.

401
00:44:02,560 --> 00:44:05,160
﻿-We'll be expecting.
-We will come.

402
00:44:05,240 --> 00:44:08,400
﻿-Have a safe journey.
-Have a safe journey.

403
00:44:08,520 --> 00:44:10,480
﻿Come on alps!

404
00:44:20,520 --> 00:44:23,000
﻿Come on!

405
00:44:49,480 --> 00:44:54,400
﻿I'll come, Osman. I will.

406
00:45:02,920 --> 00:45:09,480
Bala. You'll go to Sogut, is that so?
You have made up your mind?

407
00:45:09,600 --> 00:45:13,840
﻿I have, Osman. Don't worry about me.

408
00:45:13,920 --> 00:45:17,400
﻿-As you see, I'm alright.
-I can see it my Bala.

409
00:45:17,480 --> 00:45:20,920
﻿Of course I do, but

410
00:45:25,560 --> 00:45:28,560
﻿I miss you my Bala.

411
00:45:28,840 --> 00:45:30,880
﻿I miss you.

412
00:45:30,960 --> 00:45:34,680
With Allah's permission,
we'll be reunited soon.

413
00:45:35,160 --> 00:45:37,400
﻿I'll wait for it.

414
00:45:38,600 --> 00:45:41,120
﻿I'll wait for it.

415
00:45:41,520 --> 00:45:45,480
﻿Turahan! Send Alps after Bala.

416
00:45:45,560 --> 00:45:49,280
﻿-Infidels might do something unexpected.
-Yes, my Bey.

417
00:45:49,360 --> 00:45:52,120
﻿Alps, come on

418
00:45:52,840 --> 00:46:00,160
Come on, Osman. Have a safe journey
and good luck. Don't worry about the rest.

419
00:46:00,360 --> 00:46:05,000
﻿We'll ride our horses to our land, to Yenisehir.

420
00:46:05,160 --> 00:46:07,600
﻿Don't worry.

421
00:46:07,920 --> 00:46:11,560
﻿-May Allah protect you.
-Come on.

422
00:46:35,680 --> 00:46:37,880
﻿Yakup Bey.

423
00:46:37,960 --> 00:46:40,400
﻿You must have something on your mind,

424
00:46:40,480 --> 00:46:45,320
﻿but among all those beys who pledged loyalty to you,

425
00:46:45,680 --> 00:46:50,160
﻿-you gave the castle to Osman Bey.
-So?

426
00:46:50,920 --> 00:46:55,280
﻿-This might offend the Beys.
-Osman Bey

427
00:46:55,360 --> 00:47:01,920
fought holy wars as their age and made
the Frontiers a nightmare for the infidels.

428
00:47:02,080 --> 00:47:07,440
﻿He even lost his brothers in this cause.

429
00:47:07,800 --> 00:47:12,480
If someone gets offended
just because we showed favor

430
00:47:12,600 --> 00:47:17,920
﻿to such a Bey, let them get offended.

431
00:47:51,520 --> 00:47:56,240
﻿Osman thinks he is so smart.

432
00:47:56,320 --> 00:48:00,200
﻿He left his son in the marketplace as a spy.

433
00:48:00,360 --> 00:48:04,680
Obviously, he is wondering
why did you give the castle, my Bey.

434
00:48:04,760 --> 00:48:07,600
﻿He's not convinced.

435
00:48:08,800 --> 00:48:13,080
﻿Let him seek as long as he wants, Hatun.

436
00:48:13,280 --> 00:48:17,880
﻿I was the one who gave it. I was.

437
00:48:18,760 --> 00:48:23,840
If he doesn't obey now,
they will not be questioning my intentions,

438
00:48:24,080 --> 00:48:27,480
﻿they will be questioning his intentions.

439
00:48:27,960 --> 00:48:32,320
They will say that Osman Bey...

440
00:48:32,480 --> 00:48:35,600
...does not think about the holy case.

441
00:48:35,680 --> 00:48:39,640
﻿all he cares about is himself.

442
00:48:48,480 --> 00:48:54,040
﻿See? His followers are leaving him one by one.

443
00:48:54,160 --> 00:48:57,960
﻿He's getting lonely.

444
00:49:01,240 --> 00:49:05,000
﻿People, gather up!

445
00:49:05,160 --> 00:49:09,280
﻿Listen to me carefully.

446
00:49:09,600 --> 00:49:17,320
﻿Yakup Bey has conquered Lefke Castle.

447
00:49:18,520 --> 00:49:26,840
﻿And he gifted the castle to Osman Bey!

448
00:49:28,840 --> 00:49:33,960
﻿Let everyone know about this!

449
00:49:34,040 --> 00:49:36,800
﻿Come on!

450
00:49:39,160 --> 00:49:42,840
﻿Cerkutay is a different kind of man, Hatun.

451
00:49:42,920 --> 00:49:45,480
﻿We did very well by taking him by our side.

452
00:49:45,680 --> 00:49:48,600
﻿Let's set a table for tonight and invite him.

453
00:49:48,720 --> 00:49:52,640
﻿-We didn't get the chance to talk.
-Well thought.

454
00:49:52,920 --> 00:49:56,200
Have it prepared.

455
00:50:13,960 --> 00:50:18,080
﻿-Welcome, father.
-Thank you.

456
00:50:18,160 --> 00:50:21,760
﻿-Thank you.
I set a table for you.

457
00:50:21,840 --> 00:50:25,560
﻿I cooked half of the food myself, father.

458
00:50:27,040 --> 00:50:31,240
What did you make for your father,
tell me about it.

459
00:50:31,520 --> 00:50:35,040
﻿I made fried meat.

460
00:50:37,440 --> 00:50:40,880
﻿I made kavut as a sweetener.

461
00:50:40,960 --> 00:50:43,360
Praise be!

462
00:50:47,160 --> 00:50:49,720
﻿I cooked capitulum myself, father.

463
00:50:49,800 --> 00:50:53,720
﻿I love it. Thank you, thank you.

464
00:50:53,840 --> 00:50:56,680
﻿She is so talented, right?

465
00:50:57,040 --> 00:51:01,960
She makes it very well,
thank you my daughter.

466
00:51:02,120 --> 00:51:06,000
Come on, my beautiful daughter.
Bring the rest of them.

467
00:51:10,640 --> 00:51:14,760
She thought you'd be upset
when you hear about Lefke.

468
00:51:14,920 --> 00:51:19,280
﻿So she started making foods.

469
00:51:19,960 --> 00:51:23,400
﻿She has a clean heart, thankfully.

470
00:51:23,560 --> 00:51:27,400
﻿Come on, have a seat.

471
00:51:38,680 --> 00:51:43,200
﻿Osman Bey, what's going to happen?

472
00:51:43,440 --> 00:51:48,280
They even prevent us from gaining victories.
How it will end?

473
00:51:48,360 --> 00:51:52,480
﻿Yakup Bey is making plans in front of everyone,

474
00:51:52,640 --> 00:51:56,160
﻿but without anyone noticing it.

475
00:51:56,240 --> 00:52:00,040
Of course, he is not the only one
who is making plans.

476
00:52:00,240 --> 00:52:02,640
﻿We will make a bigger plan.

477
00:52:08,160 --> 00:52:11,400
Come on, my bey father.
The food is getting cold.

478
00:52:11,400 --> 00:52:12,520
﻿Bring it, dear.

479
00:52:13,200 --> 00:52:17,400
﻿Alright. Alright, let's start.

480
00:52:18,620 --> 00:52:20,890
Alright. Let's get started.

481
00:52:20,890 --> 00:52:21,830
In the name of Allah,
the most merciful, the most compassionate.

482
00:52:21,830 --> 00:52:23,090
Come on.

483
00:52:23,090 --> 00:52:25,190
In the name of Allah,
the most merciful, the most compassionate.

484
00:52:26,280 --> 00:52:28,480
﻿Let's start.

485
00:52:35,840 --> 00:52:38,960
Praise be!
It's so delicious.

486
00:52:40,920 --> 00:52:44,000
﻿She's her mother's daughte

487
00:52:48,080 --> 00:52:51,080
GERMIYANOGULLARI BORDER

488
00:52:51,520 --> 00:52:55,600
﻿So? Tell me, Cerkutay Bey.

489
00:52:55,680 --> 00:52:59,520
﻿What will you do to make the market flourish?

490
00:52:59,600 --> 00:53:04,720
﻿Kanyumaz will choose the alps having the gift of gab.

491
00:53:04,960 --> 00:53:11,040
And we will send the goods of our market
to caravansary in small amounts.

492
00:53:11,120 --> 00:53:15,400
﻿But we won't take money in return.

493
00:53:16,800 --> 00:53:20,560
﻿We'll give away some of the goods.

494
00:53:20,560 --> 00:53:24,080
﻿We'll make people know our goods.

495
00:53:25,120 --> 00:53:30,720
When they taste our goods,
they will flow into our market.

496
00:53:30,920 --> 00:53:34,720
﻿Then we will get much more in return.

497
00:53:34,720 --> 00:53:37,920
﻿I was right to count on your mind.

498
00:53:38,360 --> 00:53:42,800
﻿-Kanyumaz. You heard Cerkutay Bey.
-My Bey.

499
00:53:43,360 --> 00:53:46,320
﻿I heard, my Bey. As you order.

500
00:53:46,720 --> 00:53:52,320
How could Osman Bey leave a man
like you behind for all those years?

501
00:53:55,080 --> 00:53:58,320
You'll make the whole world know
about the market.

502
00:53:58,440 --> 00:54:00,360
I hope so.

503
00:54:00,600 --> 00:54:04,320
And those who didn't give you
the value you deserved...

504
00:54:04,480 --> 00:54:08,040
...will knock their heads against
the wall with regret.

505
00:54:10,040 --> 00:54:13,520
﻿Cerkutay, eat some halvah.

506
00:54:17,960 --> 00:54:21,560
﻿She was so upset with the position we gave you.

507
00:54:22,040 --> 00:54:24,640
﻿She didn't think you deserved it.

508
00:54:24,720 --> 00:54:30,760
The hatun who was under her command
for years is now almost equal to her.

509
00:54:32,480 --> 00:54:37,400
﻿-She must be surprised.
-You have a good heart, Ulgen Hatun.

510
00:54:37,560 --> 00:54:40,560
﻿You see what you want to see.

511
00:54:40,800 --> 00:54:45,920
﻿But your eyes must be open now.

512
00:54:46,040 --> 00:54:50,960
You are representing me.
You should let nobody maltreat you.

513
00:54:51,240 --> 00:54:55,400
﻿Malhun Hatun in particular.

514
00:55:14,160 --> 00:55:18,880
﻿-Come on! Come on!
-Win! Win! Win!

515
00:55:27,680 --> 00:55:35,040
﻿Stop! Not against one, Ucar. Not again!

516
00:55:35,200 --> 00:55:40,960
Take two men against you.
From the Bannerless.

517
00:55:41,480 --> 00:55:46,600
﻿Let the palace people see some strength!

518
00:55:48,800 --> 00:55:51,520
﻿-Choose!
-You.

519
00:55:52,040 --> 00:55:54,240
﻿You too.

520
00:56:01,880 --> 00:56:04,400
﻿Come on!

521
00:56:05,360 --> 00:56:09,320
﻿Even if that beast seems strong,

522
00:56:09,320 --> 00:56:13,600
﻿..he can't compete with you.

523
00:56:14,920 --> 00:56:17,400
﻿No. He's strong.

524
00:56:17,520 --> 00:56:20,960
﻿Are you afraid?

525
00:56:22,840 --> 00:56:27,080
﻿Ucar! Ucar!

526
00:56:32,160 --> 00:56:36,080
I don't know that.
But you sound so enthusiastic, Gurbuz.

527
00:56:36,160 --> 00:56:39,320
﻿-Can you beat him?
-Just wait.

528
00:56:39,360 --> 00:56:43,120
﻿I know how to beat him.

529
00:56:43,320 --> 00:56:48,680
You are so strong, huh, Bannerless?
The strength comes from mouth!

530
00:56:50,000 --> 00:56:55,200
﻿Is your mouth as strong as your muscles?

531
00:56:58,600 --> 00:57:02,080
﻿He can't even speak.

532
00:57:04,800 --> 00:57:08,600
﻿Alps, bring the molasses!

533
00:57:09,120 --> 00:57:13,400
﻿Let's see this man can compete with me...

534
00:57:13,480 --> 00:57:15,800
﻿..in the mouth race!

535
00:57:15,840 --> 00:57:19,640
﻿-Bring!
-Molasses!

536
00:57:19,840 --> 00:57:23,120
﻿Come on, bring it.

537
00:57:30,920 --> 00:57:33,720
﻿Come on, brother.

538
00:57:37,520 --> 00:57:39,020
Let's start.

539
00:57:39,350 --> 00:57:41,160
In the name of Allah,
the most merciful, the most compassionate.

540
00:57:41,160 --> 00:57:44,680
﻿Drink! Drink! Drink!

541
00:57:45,880 --> 00:57:50,920
﻿Ucar will swallow it with bones!
Molasses can do nothing to him. Come on!

542
00:58:00,520 --> 00:58:02,360
﻿I'm burning!

543
00:58:02,360 --> 00:58:07,880
﻿Don't be! We have just started! Fill it.

544
00:58:14,440 --> 00:58:20,040
Come on, Ucar. Don't disappoint us.
You swallowed a whole lamb!

545
00:58:23,840 --> 00:58:28,960
Bamsi Bey and Turgut Bey
used to compete like this too.

546
00:58:30,680 --> 00:58:33,840
﻿Bring some water! He's burning!

547
00:58:36,400 --> 00:58:40,240
﻿We are well-trained, Bannerless.

548
00:58:55,080 --> 00:59:00,080
﻿Heat the square and burn it.

549
00:59:00,440 --> 00:59:04,400
Make the Bannerless and
alps fight each other.

550
00:59:04,480 --> 00:59:07,640
﻿-Well done, brother.
-Good job, brother.

551
00:59:07,720 --> 00:59:10,480
﻿-You drank it well.
-Water.

552
00:59:10,600 --> 00:59:13,280
﻿Bring water! Water!

553
00:59:13,360 --> 00:59:15,360
﻿-Water.
-Here it is.

554
00:59:15,520 --> 00:59:18,640
﻿-Water...
-Come on, drink it.

555
00:59:18,960 --> 00:59:21,600
﻿Enough. Don't drink too much.

556
00:59:23,560 --> 00:59:27,920
﻿You're not burning yet. Not yet.

557
00:59:38,040 --> 00:59:43,720
﻿Men, Kavruk can perform a good show.

558
00:59:44,200 --> 00:59:47,600
﻿-May he?
-Go ahead.

559
00:59:47,760 --> 00:59:51,480
﻿-Kavruk, show your skills.
-Kavruk! Kavruk!

560
00:59:53,320 --> 00:59:57,320
﻿Kavruk! Kavruk!

561
01:00:32,520 --> 01:00:34,800
﻿Know your place! You are guests here!

562
01:00:34,880 --> 01:00:37,720
﻿Who will teach us? You?

563
01:00:37,800 --> 01:00:39,580
Yes!

564
01:00:40,480 --> 01:00:45,400
Bannerless, break it up.
Back, stay back.

565
01:00:48,040 --> 01:00:52,960
Know your place.
This is the palace of Bey, stop it.

566
01:00:53,120 --> 01:00:57,360
Turahan, Aykut.
If Alps do the same again, its on you.

567
01:00:57,560 --> 01:01:00,560
﻿Gurdogan, Temirboga look at me.

568
01:01:00,840 --> 01:01:04,600
The Bannerless will know their place.
They won't provoke Alps.

569
01:01:04,880 --> 01:01:07,480
﻿This is your last warning.

570
01:01:10,920 --> 01:01:13,360
﻿Now disperse.

571
01:01:18,320 --> 01:01:21,360
﻿What are you doing.

572
01:01:36,080 --> 01:01:41,080
﻿-My Shahzade, are you alright?
-I am alright Konur Bey.

573
01:01:43,400 --> 01:01:48,080
Brother, call the healers quickly.

574
01:01:48,160 --> 01:01:51,480
﻿Sister, there is no need.

575
01:01:51,560 --> 01:01:54,080
﻿Where is father?

576
01:01:54,760 --> 01:01:57,120
﻿Come, brother.

577
01:02:12,560 --> 01:02:17,000
﻿-Can I come in?
-You may enter.

578
01:02:23,640 --> 01:02:28,320
The caravan of Malhun has entered
the bazaar from another way Saadet Hatun.

579
01:02:28,400 --> 01:02:31,880
﻿They could not raid it.

580
01:02:32,840 --> 01:02:34,680
﻿Malhun.

581
01:02:34,800 --> 01:02:38,480
﻿Hold on, we arrived.

582
01:02:40,040 --> 01:02:42,880
﻿Can we come in Bey?

583
01:02:52,400 --> 01:02:56,400
﻿-Mehmet!
-Brother!

584
01:02:56,480 --> 01:02:58,240
﻿-My son! Mehmet!
-My Mehmet!

585
01:02:58,320 --> 01:03:00,280
﻿-Brother!
-Mehmet, my son!

586
01:03:00,320 --> 01:03:01,520
﻿-Brother!
-Mehmet!

587
01:03:01,600 --> 01:03:03,880
﻿-My Son!
-Mother!

588
01:03:03,960 --> 01:03:06,200
-Brother!
-Call a healer!

589
01:03:06,360 --> 01:03:08,560
-Alps!
-There are no healers.

590
01:03:08,680 --> 01:03:11,680
﻿-They went to Germiyan in the morning.
-Fitnat!

591
01:03:11,840 --> 01:03:14,280
Go call a healer!

592
01:03:14,880 --> 01:03:19,200
﻿My valiant. Yakup Bey..

593
01:03:19,600 --> 01:03:21,200
Mehmet, son!

594
01:03:22,720 --> 01:03:25,480
﻿-Yakup Bey.
-Mehmet!

595
01:03:25,640 --> 01:03:29,800
﻿Yakup Bey.

596
01:03:30,600 --> 01:03:35,480
Careful Baysungur. Make no mistakes.
It is the order of Malhun Hatun.

597
01:03:35,640 --> 01:03:39,040
﻿Do not worry my Shahzade.
All rugs are carried.

598
01:03:39,200 --> 01:03:42,800
﻿-I will have the ones in cart on display.
-Alright.

599
01:03:44,000 --> 01:03:49,760
﻿-Make them keep watch for two weeks.
-As you command my Shahzade.

600
01:03:51,200 --> 01:03:55,120
﻿-Alaeddin.
-Gonca Hatun, what happened?

601
01:03:55,240 --> 01:03:59,000
My brother is wounded.
We need your help Alaeddin Bey.

602
01:03:59,840 --> 01:04:02,320
﻿Quickly.

603
01:04:09,080 --> 01:04:12,160
﻿Bey, I have great news.

604
01:04:12,320 --> 01:04:16,480
-I got the treasure.
-Praise be!

605
01:04:17,320 --> 01:04:23,040
-And? What happened to you?
-However..

606
01:04:23,720 --> 01:04:28,880
﻿-I hit Mehmet, Bey.
-You did what?

607
01:04:30,400 --> 01:04:35,080
What did you do my son?
Does he live? Did he see you?

608
01:04:35,200 --> 01:04:37,360
﻿I don't know how he is.

609
01:04:37,440 --> 01:04:39,040
﻿-I stepped on him.
-Orhan.

610
01:04:39,120 --> 01:04:41,240
﻿Bey, I checked..

611
01:04:41,360 --> 01:04:45,680
He was alive.
And that savage can take it.

612
01:04:47,920 --> 01:04:51,360
﻿-Tell me what happened.
-Mehmet.

613
01:04:51,600 --> 01:04:56,400
Made the bannerless wear crusader
outfit and pointed them to our way.

614
01:04:56,720 --> 01:05:02,200
I hit them with their own trickery.
They think Mongols hit them.

615
01:05:08,800 --> 01:05:11,640
﻿Dumrul, come here.

616
01:05:11,800 --> 01:05:14,680
﻿-Bey.
-Go to the frontier bazaar.

617
01:05:14,840 --> 01:05:18,960
﻿-Check his situation.
-As you command, Bey.

618
01:05:22,600 --> 01:05:25,880
﻿Thanks to Holofira.

619
01:05:26,680 --> 01:05:29,280
﻿She never left beside me.

620
01:05:33,960 --> 01:05:37,280
﻿Thanks to your heart my girl.

621
01:05:41,280 --> 01:05:44,560
﻿Since the danger on the road is no more.

622
01:05:44,640 --> 01:05:48,040
﻿Then Holofira can return to her home.

623
01:05:48,200 --> 01:05:53,120
﻿-Mother, this is not the time to..
-Yes.

624
01:05:53,200 --> 01:05:56,200
﻿I want to return to my home as well.

625
01:05:56,640 --> 01:06:00,720
Then as you wish, my girl.
You can depart in the morning.

626
01:06:00,840 --> 01:06:04,280
﻿Alps will accompany you to your home.

627
01:06:04,680 --> 01:06:07,600
﻿If you'll excuse me.

628
01:06:13,760 --> 01:06:20,000
Father, if you allow me,
I want to accompany her as well.

629
01:06:20,080 --> 01:06:25,160
You accompanied Holofira enough.
She will go with Alps, you'll come to bazaar with us.

630
01:06:25,240 --> 01:06:27,720
﻿-Mother.
-My son.

631
01:06:29,640 --> 01:06:33,000
﻿Don't make your mother say it twice.

632
01:06:34,840 --> 01:06:37,600
﻿As you command, Bey.

633
01:06:37,840 --> 01:06:40,760
﻿If you'll excuse me.

634
01:06:45,880 --> 01:06:49,560
﻿I understand that mother does not want Holofira..

635
01:06:49,760 --> 01:06:54,400
﻿-However, you were not this cruel Bey Father.
-Look at her.

636
01:06:56,000 --> 01:06:59,560
﻿Look what she's saying to her father.

637
01:07:00,040 --> 01:07:03,800
﻿Fatma, my dear daughte

638
01:07:04,840 --> 01:07:08,600
﻿Love is the greatest challenge for humans.

639
01:07:08,680 --> 01:07:10,880
﻿Let us wait first.

640
01:07:11,000 --> 01:07:14,560
﻿If your brother's love is just eagerness..

641
01:07:14,640 --> 01:07:17,440
﻿Or real, we will see.

642
01:07:24,120 --> 01:07:26,520
﻿Orhan Bey.

643
01:07:26,520 --> 01:07:29,480
﻿So it is time.

644
01:07:29,680 --> 01:07:32,280
﻿I am finally returning home.

645
01:07:32,720 --> 01:07:38,160
﻿Holofira. I do not want you to go.

646
01:07:39,760 --> 01:07:43,240
﻿Only you want me here, Orhan.

647
01:07:44,320 --> 01:07:50,600
Your family think the same as me.
My departure will be good for all of us.

648
01:07:51,160 --> 01:07:53,920
﻿If you want to stay.

649
01:07:54,320 --> 01:07:59,920
And if the problem is only
my mother, I will convince her.

650
01:08:10,840 --> 01:08:14,240
﻿I want to go, Orhan.

651
01:08:17,240 --> 01:08:19,399
﻿Maybe..

652
01:08:20,479 --> 01:08:24,279
﻿If we met on different terms..

653
01:08:25,840 --> 01:08:27,960
﻿Maybe..

654
01:08:31,720 --> 01:08:36,800
-Whatever, take care of yourself.
-Holofira.

655
01:08:51,359 --> 01:08:55,530
I...
always...

656
01:09:39,359 --> 01:09:43,359
﻿Do not make me suffer more.

657
01:09:47,600 --> 01:09:50,240
﻿My destiny brought you to me.

658
01:09:55,640 --> 01:10:00,000
﻿I will always wait for you, Lord's daughter.

659
01:10:07,880 --> 01:10:14,040
﻿Malhun... Malhun.

660
01:10:14,120 --> 01:10:18,960
What if he really loves her?
What are we going to do then?

661
01:10:19,080 --> 01:10:23,680
-You know he is stubborn.
-No. Marry him with someone as soon as possible.

662
01:10:24,280 --> 01:10:27,360
﻿We will find brides for both Orhan and Alaeddin.

663
01:10:27,480 --> 01:10:32,600
-Fatma. Keep your eyes open.
-For my Alaeddin brother as well?

664
01:10:35,720 --> 01:10:40,240
﻿Look... What is wrong, Fatma?

665
01:10:41,240 --> 01:10:45,200
-Do you know something?
-No, my Bey father.

666
01:10:45,320 --> 01:10:50,120
I am surprised because both of my brothers
are going to get married at the same time.

667
01:10:50,600 --> 01:10:54,520
Don't worry.
I'll look around.

668
01:10:59,040 --> 01:11:01,360
﻿Good then.

669
01:11:06,640 --> 01:11:11,320
﻿Hang on, my valiant.
Hang on, my son.

670
01:11:24,280 --> 01:11:26,880
﻿Hang on.

671
01:11:29,240 --> 01:11:34,160
Yakup Bey! Stop.
We have to examine the wound first.

672
01:11:37,400 --> 01:11:43,760
-Can you do it, Alaeddin Bey?
-Trust me. We don't have enough time.

673
01:11:46,040 --> 01:11:51,200
He is losing too much blood.
We need a healer, Yakup Bey.

674
01:11:51,400 --> 01:11:56,000
-Send news to everywhere!
-Mother, we don't have enough time!

675
01:11:56,080 --> 01:11:59,600
﻿Father! I trust Alaeddin Bey doubtlessly.

676
01:11:59,840 --> 01:12:02,120
﻿Please, move. We don't have time!

677
01:12:02,240 --> 01:12:05,480
﻿-Gonca!
-Mother, come on!

678
01:12:07,280 --> 01:12:09,840
﻿Come.

679
01:12:13,280 --> 01:12:16,240
﻿The wound is clean. There is no poison.

680
01:12:16,520 --> 01:12:20,440
﻿It doesn't seem deep. Baysungur, the bag!

681
01:12:21,040 --> 01:12:24,280
﻿Gonca Hatun. Prepare a cup.

682
01:12:24,400 --> 01:12:27,360
﻿He'll be alright, right?

683
01:12:29,400 --> 01:12:31,760
Hang on, Mehmet.

684
01:12:32,880 --> 01:12:35,800
﻿Hang on.

685
01:12:37,240 --> 01:12:40,640
Gonca Hatun.
Clean the wound.

686
01:12:42,440 --> 01:12:45,760
﻿Tell me something, Alaeddin. Will he be alright?

687
01:12:45,840 --> 01:12:52,080
He lost too much blood.
He is weak right now, but his wound is not deadly.

688
01:12:57,000 --> 01:12:59,520
-Kanyumaz!
-My Bey...

689
01:12:59,640 --> 01:13:03,280
﻿Find the one who shed my son's blood!

690
01:13:09,880 --> 01:13:12,800
﻿Hang on Mehmed Bey. Hang on.

691
01:13:12,960 --> 01:13:16,640
O Healer! O Healer!

692
01:13:16,880 --> 01:13:20,040
In the name of Allah,
the most merciful, the most compassionate.

693
01:13:25,000 --> 01:13:27,980
O Healer! O Healer!

694
01:13:28,450 --> 01:13:31,070
In the name of Allah,
the most merciful, the most compassionate.

695
01:13:38,560 --> 01:13:41,680
Saadet Hatun.
Tell them to prepare sherbet for his blood loss.

696
01:13:41,760 --> 01:13:45,960
﻿I'll do it for my son. Come on, Fitnat.

697
01:13:46,200 --> 01:13:50,000
When we also prepare a soup with broth,
my lion will get better.

698
01:13:50,240 --> 01:13:54,880
﻿My son will recover. Come on Fitnat.

699
01:13:59,600 --> 01:14:03,480
Don't be afraid.
He'll be alright if Allah permits.

700
01:14:04,280 --> 01:14:07,160
If Allah permits.

701
01:14:10,840 --> 01:14:13,360
-He'll be alright.
-Thank you.

702
01:14:17,560 --> 01:14:19,080
﻿Master Gera.

703
01:14:20,160 --> 01:14:22,480
﻿You came with your light.

704
01:14:39,560 --> 01:14:41,960
﻿Stand up, Vasilis.

705
01:15:03,840 --> 01:15:08,000
-It's been a long time, Master Gera...
-Ah, time...

706
01:15:08,360 --> 01:15:12,000
﻿But you made use of that time very well.

707
01:15:12,160 --> 01:15:15,000
﻿You surrounded them from all sides.

708
01:15:15,200 --> 01:15:18,920
﻿You lit the first sparkle by killing Mesud.

709
01:15:19,120 --> 01:15:24,120
﻿Now we will start a big fire, Vasilis.

710
01:15:24,200 --> 01:15:26,080
﻿Thanks to your light, Master Gera.

711
01:15:26,160 --> 01:15:29,680
﻿Tell me about Osman's palace, Vasilis.

712
01:15:30,640 --> 01:15:36,040
﻿The people he trusts the most... Tell me, Vasilis.

713
01:15:36,320 --> 01:15:41,440
He has Alps and Beys
who are even more loyal than apostles.

714
01:15:42,560 --> 01:15:45,920
﻿They are becoming a shield around Osman.

715
01:15:46,840 --> 01:15:49,000
﻿A shield..

716
01:15:49,240 --> 01:15:52,440
﻿We made a hole in that shield.

717
01:15:52,960 --> 01:15:55,000
﻿Cerkutay.

718
01:15:56,520 --> 01:16:00,520
﻿But we will destroy that shield.

719
01:16:00,640 --> 01:16:02,600
﻿Konur Bey..

720
01:16:03,400 --> 01:16:07,600
...is leading Osman's army,
he is Osman's sword.

721
01:16:07,680 --> 01:16:10,600
﻿I gained his trust when I killed Remus.

722
01:16:10,800 --> 01:16:13,840
-Who else?
-Bayindir Bey.

723
01:16:14,040 --> 01:16:19,560
﻿He is responsible of Osman's treasure and gold.

724
01:16:21,880 --> 01:16:25,680
-Who else?
-Boran Bey.

725
01:16:26,240 --> 01:16:29,320
﻿He is Osman's closed book.

726
01:16:30,880 --> 01:16:35,240
﻿He can die for his Bey without hesitation.
He is loyal...

727
01:16:35,840 --> 01:16:38,600
﻿...he is in charge of the palace's order.

728
01:16:39,040 --> 01:16:41,880
﻿Especially its security.

729
01:16:44,880 --> 01:16:47,800
﻿Our target is Boran.

730
01:16:49,560 --> 01:16:54,160
﻿First... we will take him.

731
01:16:55,080 --> 01:17:00,040
﻿The palace will be defenseless. Osman...

732
01:17:00,720 --> 01:17:06,080
﻿...will stumble, he'll make a mistake.

733
01:17:09,760 --> 01:17:13,480
Atmaca and the Bannerless
under his command...

734
01:17:13,600 --> 01:17:16,160
﻿...they are loyal to us.

735
01:17:16,320 --> 01:17:19,240
﻿We can defeat Boran anytime we want..

736
01:17:19,360 --> 01:17:23,600
﻿...and ruin Osman's palace.

737
01:17:27,000 --> 01:17:29,800
﻿The Bannerless, huh?

738
01:18:11,160 --> 01:18:17,080
﻿Yakup Bey is covering up his tracks.

739
01:18:18,760 --> 01:18:22,120
Are you thinking about what our move
is going to be, my Osman?

740
01:18:22,200 --> 01:18:24,000
﻿Right.

741
01:18:25,440 --> 01:18:30,480
But peace and union must be
present at the frontiers.

742
01:18:31,440 --> 01:18:34,160
﻿Therefore..

743
01:18:35,320 --> 01:18:40,440
﻿...if we need to obey Yakup Bey...
-Obey?

744
01:18:41,120 --> 01:18:45,360
That's why Yakup Bey is playing
all those games.

745
01:18:47,920 --> 01:18:51,280
﻿You are thinking about something else.

746
01:18:51,680 --> 01:18:54,880
﻿You make your preparations.

747
01:18:55,120 --> 01:18:57,120
﻿Don't worry.

748
01:19:02,760 --> 01:19:05,760
GERMIYANOGULLARI BORDER

749
01:19:18,800 --> 01:19:21,800
﻿I owe you a life, Scholar.

750
01:19:23,200 --> 01:19:29,160
-My Alps...
-Brother?

751
01:19:29,600 --> 01:19:32,640
﻿Brother?

752
01:19:35,440 --> 01:19:38,880
﻿-My Alps...
-He is waking up.

753
01:19:38,960 --> 01:19:43,240
-My Alps...
-Thank to Allah.

754
01:19:43,640 --> 01:19:46,800
﻿Good... Good.

755
01:19:52,960 --> 01:19:57,880
You are too tired.
It will strengthen you as well.

756
01:19:58,800 --> 01:20:00,920
﻿Thank you.

757
01:20:04,040 --> 01:20:06,960
In the name of Allah,
the most merciful, the most compassionate.

758
01:20:28,360 --> 01:20:32,840
﻿Father... My brother is waking up!

759
01:20:35,240 --> 01:20:37,240
﻿Mehmed!

760
01:20:37,760 --> 01:20:42,680
-Father...
-Thank to Allah, my son.

761
01:20:43,360 --> 01:20:47,400
﻿My strong son... My lion son..

762
01:20:47,560 --> 01:20:51,520
-Mother...
-He must drink his sherbet.

763
01:20:51,640 --> 01:20:53,680
﻿My Mehmed..

764
01:20:54,920 --> 01:20:57,800
I boiled healing herbs and
put it in this bottle.

765
01:20:59,040 --> 01:21:02,280
﻿This will take his pain away InshaAllah.

766
01:21:02,440 --> 01:21:05,320
﻿Thank you Alaeddin Bey.

767
01:21:19,000 --> 01:21:22,600
﻿My Mehmed, I am here.

768
01:21:25,800 --> 01:21:29,240
﻿I will not forget this favor, Alaeddin Bey.

769
01:21:29,320 --> 01:21:33,720
﻿Now, Germiyan owes you a life.

770
01:21:34,320 --> 01:21:37,120
﻿Kanyumaz!

771
01:21:50,760 --> 01:21:53,400
﻿Take it.

772
01:21:53,720 --> 01:21:57,840
No thank you, Yakup Bey.
I did my duty.

773
01:21:58,000 --> 01:22:02,120
There is no need for a gift.
Thank you.

774
01:22:02,200 --> 01:22:05,360
﻿You are both brave..

775
01:22:05,960 --> 01:22:09,560
﻿...and pure-hearted, huh?

776
01:22:10,560 --> 01:22:15,720
﻿It is apparent that you are Sheikh Edebali's grandson.

777
01:22:17,560 --> 01:22:19,800
﻿Thank you.

778
01:22:20,200 --> 01:22:24,800
It's alright, Yakup Bey, it's alright.

779
01:22:51,120 --> 01:22:54,880
With Allah's mercy and grace,
peace be upon you.

780
01:22:55,080 --> 01:22:58,040
Peace be upon you too.

781
01:23:02,640 --> 01:23:06,560
﻿-Welcome, Ayhan Bey.
-Thank you.

782
01:23:07,640 --> 01:23:11,840
﻿Make way! Osman Bey!

783
01:23:30,160 --> 01:23:34,600
﻿Welcome. Is your caravan safe?

784
01:23:34,680 --> 01:23:38,680
﻿-How are the children, are they well.
-May Allah bless you.

785
01:23:38,840 --> 01:23:42,520
﻿Thankfully, they are alright, we are so relieved.

786
01:23:42,600 --> 01:23:49,640
Good, good. So, we heard about you.
You have visited Yenisehir downtown.

787
01:23:54,120 --> 01:23:58,400
I have, Osman Bey. Praise be.

788
01:23:58,520 --> 01:24:02,120
It's has nothing less than
the markets in Konya.

789
01:24:02,200 --> 01:24:06,320
If you'll excuse me, I'd like to trade
with a few shopkeepers.

790
01:24:06,400 --> 01:24:13,400
Is that so? Then let me introduce
you to Bayindir Bey.

791
01:24:13,800 --> 01:24:16,960
He is responsible for the order
of Yenisehir's downtown.

792
01:24:17,240 --> 01:24:19,520
﻿He is very good at it. Thank you.

793
01:24:19,640 --> 01:24:21,880
Thank you.

794
01:24:22,080 --> 01:24:26,640
﻿My Bey orders and I do my duty.

795
01:24:29,380 --> 01:24:32,120
Ayhan Agha will come to the
Frontier marketplace with us.

796
01:24:32,230 --> 01:24:34,570
You will introduce him to
the shopkeepers there.

797
01:24:34,720 --> 01:24:37,880
Sure, my Bey.

798
01:24:38,240 --> 01:24:39,180
My Bey.

799
01:24:52,680 --> 01:24:57,160
﻿My Bey, ten thousand gold has been loaded to the cars.

800
01:24:57,400 --> 01:25:00,000
﻿The rest has been delivered to the treasury.

801
01:25:00,240 --> 01:25:04,120
﻿With Allah's permission, the Germiyan marketplace

802
01:25:04,160 --> 01:25:06,720
﻿will witness a glory it has never seen before.

803
01:25:06,720 --> 01:25:09,640
Praise be! Praise be!
Thank you.

804
01:25:11,960 --> 01:25:15,240
﻿-Boran.
-My Bey.

805
01:25:16,360 --> 01:25:21,320
I don't want a single breach of security in the palace.
You are responsible for the security.

806
01:25:21,320 --> 01:25:25,400
﻿-I'll do my best, my Bey.
-I don't want any mistake.

807
01:25:29,920 --> 01:25:34,040
﻿Come on. We'll go to the Frontier's marketplace.

808
01:25:35,120 --> 01:25:38,040
﻿Osman Bey.

809
01:25:38,320 --> 01:25:42,400
﻿Give us orders too. We don't want to be out of practice.

810
01:25:42,680 --> 01:25:46,920
﻿Let us fight, let us raid.

811
01:25:48,640 --> 01:25:52,480
﻿You want war, is that so?

812
01:25:57,560 --> 01:26:01,960
﻿What do you have on your mind? To where?

813
01:26:02,040 --> 01:26:06,200
-Whatever you wish, Osman Bey.
-No.

814
01:26:11,600 --> 01:26:14,640
﻿Go to the outpost.

815
01:26:16,440 --> 01:26:20,000
﻿Konur, Turahan.

816
01:26:20,200 --> 01:26:26,560
﻿-You will go to the outpost with them.
-Yes, my Bey.

817
01:27:06,480 --> 01:27:09,840
﻿Bala, do you want something?

818
01:27:10,280 --> 01:27:13,040
﻿Now..

819
01:27:15,640 --> 01:27:19,800
﻿...I only have my Alaeddin with me.

820
01:27:24,600 --> 01:27:27,440
But it seems...

821
01:27:28,120 --> 01:27:33,240
...he will still have a mother.
-Shush, Bala.

822
01:27:33,320 --> 01:27:37,080
﻿Don't say that. Don't.

823
01:27:37,240 --> 01:27:40,320
﻿Protect him.

824
01:27:40,480 --> 01:27:43,680
﻿I trust him to you, Malh

825
01:27:43,880 --> 01:27:47,400
﻿I trust him to you.

826
01:27:47,600 --> 01:27:50,840
﻿-Bala.
-Don't get closer.

827
01:27:58,560 --> 01:28:01,280
﻿Promise me.

828
01:28:03,880 --> 01:28:07,920
﻿I promise you, Bala.
I promise you.

829
01:28:15,160 --> 01:28:18,880
﻿You kept that promise very well.

830
01:28:18,960 --> 01:28:23,600
﻿You protected my trust, Malhun.
-Bala.

831
01:28:23,920 --> 01:28:27,960
Thank my Creator that you are alright.

832
01:28:28,080 --> 01:28:30,480
﻿I'm alright.

833
01:28:30,840 --> 01:28:35,640
﻿Your test was so harsh Bala.

834
01:28:35,760 --> 01:28:39,880
﻿We have passed those tests all together, Malhun.

835
01:28:40,440 --> 01:28:44,080
﻿Come on, come.

836
01:28:49,600 --> 01:28:53,040
﻿How are you? How are the children?

837
01:28:53,200 --> 01:28:56,440
﻿Don't ask about it Bala.

838
01:28:56,560 --> 01:29:01,080
﻿They grow and their problems grow as well.

839
01:29:01,240 --> 01:29:05,880
﻿You must have heard Holofira is back.

840
01:29:05,960 --> 01:29:10,120
﻿It seems Orhan still loves Holofira.

841
01:29:10,320 --> 01:29:13,480
﻿-So she will be the bride?
-May Allah forbid.

842
01:29:13,640 --> 01:29:19,120
She can't be the bride. Holofira will go
back to her home before it gets any longer.

843
01:29:19,200 --> 01:29:22,720
﻿They must have set out already.

844
01:29:22,840 --> 01:29:28,560
But you say he loves her.
How are we going to stop Orhan?

845
01:29:30,200 --> 01:29:33,120
﻿I have something
on my mind, but...

846
01:29:33,280 --> 01:29:40,520
﻿I think we should find someone for Orhan and Alaeddin.

847
01:29:42,120 --> 01:29:46,160
﻿So you only want daughter of Beys.

848
01:29:46,960 --> 01:29:49,920
﻿You talked about the test just now,

849
01:29:50,120 --> 01:29:55,560
﻿you know why I accepted such a big test, Bala.

850
01:29:55,640 --> 01:29:58,760
﻿I saw a dream with Osman Bey.

851
01:29:59,400 --> 01:30:04,440
﻿Of course, nothing we went through was easy, but

852
01:30:05,040 --> 01:30:11,800
we both suffered this test for
the dream we saw in Osman Bey.

853
01:30:11,960 --> 01:30:15,800
﻿And we're still enduring it.

854
01:30:16,000 --> 01:30:22,320
Now we need daughters-in-law
who will keep this dream just like we do.

855
01:30:22,400 --> 01:30:27,040
﻿You are right. Let's take a look around, then.

856
01:30:27,160 --> 01:30:30,720
﻿I'll inform the Hatuns.

857
01:30:30,800 --> 01:30:35,320
I should get going, Bala. Yakup Bey invited me
to the marketplace, I shouldn't be late.

858
01:30:35,480 --> 01:30:39,800
About the marketplace,
what did Osman Bey decide on?

859
01:30:40,000 --> 01:30:44,840
﻿I guess he will be by Yakup Bey's side.

860
01:30:45,400 --> 01:30:50,280
-What do you think?
-I don't know Bala.

861
01:30:50,360 --> 01:30:55,080
It seems the fact that Yakup Bey is fighting
holy wars convinced Osman Bey.

862
01:30:55,200 --> 01:31:00,200
He fights holy wars but at the same time
he makes all sorts of plans behind us.

863
01:31:00,440 --> 01:31:07,600
I know. I know but I guess Osman Bey
has something on his mind.

864
01:31:21,160 --> 01:31:24,760
﻿I'm waiting for your orders, sir.

865
01:31:24,960 --> 01:31:30,800
Get ready, Atmaca.
We'll take the gold back from Osman.

866
01:31:31,000 --> 01:31:38,240
﻿Gather the bannerless ones who are loyal to us.

867
01:31:38,400 --> 01:31:44,240
I know, master Vasilis.
We will be even faster than the wind.

868
01:31:53,560 --> 01:31:56,360
﻿May it be easy.

869
01:31:59,800 --> 01:32:07,080
In love's market, lives in display,
mine I offer, but none to convey.

870
01:32:07,200 --> 01:32:13,680
They proclaim the death of lover,
yet it is the nafs that die...

871
01:32:13,840 --> 01:32:17,880
﻿lovers do not die.

872
01:32:21,840 --> 01:32:26,360
They think they are dead,
yet they wander, even bolder

873
01:32:26,440 --> 01:32:30,960
they let the nafs win the fight
the lover's warmth grows colder.

874
01:32:31,360 --> 01:32:35,000
Welcome, Dervish.

875
01:32:36,080 --> 01:32:42,280
So the reputation of our marketplace
even reached to the guild.

876
01:32:42,600 --> 01:32:47,280
﻿The reputation of your marketplace.
Yes, it did.

877
01:32:47,480 --> 01:32:53,040
Where are you coming from?
What do you want to buy, let me help you.

878
01:32:53,240 --> 01:32:55,400
﻿I come from Hayy

879
01:32:55,520 --> 01:33:01,040
﻿But I'm not here to buy, I'm here to sell.
-To sell?

880
01:33:03,320 --> 01:33:09,160
﻿Which counter did we give? What do you sell?

881
01:33:10,480 --> 01:33:13,280
﻿I'm here to sell lives, but

882
01:33:13,360 --> 01:33:16,640
﻿lives are sold in the marketplace of love.

883
01:33:16,720 --> 01:33:22,800
﻿It seems this is just the marketplace of wrath and ambition.

884
01:33:22,920 --> 01:33:27,840
﻿I can't set a counter here for life.

885
01:33:28,600 --> 01:33:32,880
What wrath, what ambition did you see here,
Dervish Effendi.

886
01:33:32,960 --> 01:33:35,840
﻿What else can be found in the place of living ones?

887
01:33:35,880 --> 01:33:39,120
﻿You are looking for dead men in the marketplace.

888
01:33:39,200 --> 01:33:42,240
﻿The dead is in the tomb.

889
01:33:42,360 --> 01:33:49,120
In human, there are two beings.
One is the skin and the other one is the life.

890
01:33:49,360 --> 01:33:54,920
The skin belongs to this world and
the life belongs both of the worlds.

891
01:33:55,640 --> 01:34:00,800
﻿Sultan of the worlds Rasulullah (PBUH)

892
01:34:01,080 --> 01:34:07,480
﻿says that "Before you die, you shall die."

893
01:34:07,960 --> 01:34:13,720
﻿Skin shall be alive, you should kill your nafs.

894
01:34:16,680 --> 01:34:21,560
The one that dies before he dies
knows that he is incapable.

895
01:34:22,080 --> 01:34:28,480
﻿This world is a guestroom and this skin is a trust.

896
01:34:29,640 --> 01:34:33,600
﻿If human does not die before he dies,

897
01:34:33,800 --> 01:34:40,120
he wanders around on earth,
he says "I can break the ground"

898
01:34:40,200 --> 01:34:43,720
"I can climb up to that mountain."

899
01:34:44,200 --> 01:34:48,360
﻿He gets angry, gets ambitious.

900
01:34:51,760 --> 01:34:55,520
﻿His pride becomes his master.

901
01:34:56,040 --> 01:35:00,600
The marketplace of those who killed
their nafs is the marketplace of love,

902
01:35:00,680 --> 01:35:04,560
and the marketplace of those
who are the slaves of their nafs

903
01:35:04,760 --> 01:35:08,200
﻿is the marketplace of wrath. So,

904
01:35:08,400 --> 01:35:14,760
in the tombs, there are those whose skins are dead
but we are looking for those who killed their nafs.

905
01:35:15,480 --> 01:35:18,160
﻿But it seems

906
01:35:18,240 --> 01:35:23,840
﻿no one here wants to die before he dies.

907
01:35:24,960 --> 01:35:27,120
See you.

908
01:35:32,760 --> 01:35:38,440
Don't let me lose sight of who I am,
Greed clouds my vision,

909
01:35:38,840 --> 01:35:45,520
The earth's cycle, in constant flow,
Good and bad arrive, then they go.

910
01:35:46,160 --> 01:35:52,720
﻿In the hereafter, one hopes and prays

911
01:35:52,880 --> 01:35:59,840
But a dervish Yunus says,
"The Eternal is here, and here He lays"

912
01:36:02,960 --> 01:36:05,240
﻿Before you die,

913
01:36:06,880 --> 01:36:09,320
﻿..you shall die.

914
01:36:52,400 --> 01:36:55,360
﻿My Bey, welcome.

915
01:36:55,360 --> 01:36:59,520
﻿-Thank you.
-This is our place.

916
01:37:00,000 --> 01:37:04,520
﻿-Welcome, my Bey.
Thank you, son. Thank you.

917
01:37:04,600 --> 01:37:08,480
﻿This is it, huh?

918
01:37:13,120 --> 01:37:19,120
﻿O people! Hear ye! Hear ye!

919
01:37:19,520 --> 01:37:27,560
Here is Osman Bey's gift! Those having a son
shall not be upset for not being able to have a wedding!

920
01:37:27,880 --> 01:37:33,060
Those having a daughter shall not be upset
for not being able to prepare dowry!

921
01:37:33,170 --> 01:37:35,970
Everybody in debt, gather up!

922
01:37:48,280 --> 01:37:52,600
-May Allah be pleased with Osman Bey.
-Thank you.

923
01:37:53,840 --> 01:37:57,800
﻿He's here! Osman Bey is here!

924
01:37:58,160 --> 01:38:01,960
﻿Oh, my Cerkutay.

925
01:38:11,400 --> 01:38:14,680
﻿Look. Look at me.

926
01:38:14,960 --> 01:38:19,760
﻿-Have you grown tall?
Yes, my Bey. Can I be an alp now?

927
01:38:19,760 --> 01:38:26,000
Be patient.
You need some more time to be an alp.

928
01:38:26,640 --> 01:38:31,600
Look at me. Praise be.
You will grow fast.

929
01:38:31,680 --> 01:38:34,880
﻿I miss you so much, my Bey.

930
01:38:37,480 --> 01:38:40,120
﻿Me too, boy.

931
01:38:43,840 --> 01:38:47,520
﻿Me too. Come on.

932
01:38:47,640 --> 01:38:52,000
﻿-Let me show you around the market, Osman Bey.
-Alright.

933
01:38:55,000 --> 01:39:00,600
﻿Good. Good, good. Order!

934
01:39:00,880 --> 01:39:06,320
Order matters! I don't want to see
these sacks here again. Come on!

935
01:39:09,960 --> 01:39:15,600
﻿Cerkutay, Osman Bey is here.

936
01:39:18,040 --> 01:39:23,160
﻿Don't, Ulgen. Don't let him maltreat you.

937
01:39:25,560 --> 01:39:31,640
﻿Come on. Let's go say welcome to Osman Bey.

938
01:39:40,680 --> 01:39:43,200
﻿What do you think about the market?

939
01:39:43,200 --> 01:39:47,320
﻿Well... The market
can grow easily.

940
01:39:47,480 --> 01:39:54,040
But what matters is its location.
It's on the road linking the west with the east.

941
01:39:54,280 --> 01:40:00,080
It's near Yalakova Port.
Yakup Bey chose a right spot.

942
01:40:00,600 --> 01:40:04,720
You say it will make those who
sell goods here grow bigger too, huh?

943
01:40:04,880 --> 01:40:14,240
﻿Yes, but what matters is who it will make grow with it.

944
01:40:17,120 --> 01:40:21,560
﻿Fine. Let's see the stands.

945
01:40:21,680 --> 01:40:25,200
Peace be upon you! Good day!

946
01:40:26,840 --> 01:40:33,880
You'll enter Osman's palace as servants.
We'll take all his gold.

947
01:40:34,160 --> 01:40:38,280
﻿-We will!
-And vengeance..

948
01:40:41,440 --> 01:40:46,320
﻿We will hit Boran who Osman trusts most...

949
01:40:46,640 --> 01:40:50,680
﻿...in his palace which he feels safest.

950
01:40:53,720 --> 01:40:57,400
﻿Osman will lose another part of his.

951
01:40:58,840 --> 01:41:03,680
﻿-He will lose his sleep.
-Sir.

952
01:41:05,080 --> 01:41:12,800
How will we get rid of Osman's men?
They will want to check the chests.

953
01:41:15,200 --> 01:41:20,000
﻿Putting those fools to sleep is my job, Atmaca.

954
01:41:20,840 --> 01:41:23,840
﻿You finish your preparations.

955
01:41:24,600 --> 01:41:29,280
Today, we are going to destroy
Osman's palace.

956
01:41:39,760 --> 01:41:45,000
-Have a good one!
-May Allah be please with you, my Bey.

957
01:41:45,120 --> 01:41:47,880
﻿-May Allah be pleased with you too.
-Thanks, my Bey.

958
01:41:47,920 --> 01:41:53,280
Thank you too.
Thank you! Thank you!

959
01:41:59,880 --> 01:42:05,080
Welcome, Osman... Bey.

960
01:42:06,400 --> 01:42:12,160
Thank you, Cerkutay......... Bey.

961
01:42:22,240 --> 01:42:25,520
﻿This duty looks good on you.

962
01:42:28,480 --> 01:42:30,800
﻿You deserve this.

963
01:42:31,960 --> 01:42:36,320
﻿Yakup Bey gave me this title, thankfully.

964
01:42:45,720 --> 01:42:51,280
-Cerkutay, come here. Don't disturb Osman Bey.
-No.

965
01:42:51,720 --> 01:42:57,920
﻿-I missed Osman Bey. I'll stay with him.
-Oh, boy...

966
01:42:59,360 --> 01:43:04,040
﻿-Cerkutay.
-Just wait.

967
01:43:06,680 --> 01:43:09,840
﻿Just wait.

968
01:43:16,120 --> 01:43:21,080
﻿Boy, you should go now.

969
01:43:22,760 --> 01:43:29,760
﻿-I will come again, my Bey. Don't worry.
-Of course. Whenever you want.

970
01:43:48,040 --> 01:43:50,600
﻿Ayhan Agha.

971
01:43:50,960 --> 01:43:54,720
You say this market will make
the sellers grow bigger, huh?

972
01:43:54,720 --> 01:43:59,560
Yes, Osman Bey.
I'm a tradesman of this time.

973
01:43:59,680 --> 01:44:04,640
When I look, I can see the earning
and loss from a distance.

974
01:44:04,960 --> 01:44:10,240
﻿I want this market to make you grow.
I owe you a life.

975
01:44:10,520 --> 01:44:14,000
﻿Well... What should we do then?

976
01:44:14,040 --> 01:44:23,040
It's your decision. But if I were you,
I would buy at least the half of this market.

977
01:44:29,480 --> 01:44:37,680
Hey, you are convincing!
You'll almost make me buy the whole market.

978
01:44:39,880 --> 01:44:42,720
﻿Now tell me.

979
01:44:44,360 --> 01:44:50,760
﻿Is this for your interest or my interest?

980
01:44:51,600 --> 01:44:55,600
﻿For the interest of both of us, Osman Bey.

981
01:45:08,920 --> 01:45:14,080
﻿Good. Good.

982
01:45:18,160 --> 01:45:21,760
-Thank you.
-Thank you, thank you.

983
01:45:22,040 --> 01:45:26,280
﻿Thank you! Thank you!

984
01:45:41,080 --> 01:45:45,880
﻿-You should rest more, Mehmed.
-I'm good, mother.

985
01:45:46,120 --> 01:45:51,320
If jackals see the wolf wounded,
they become willing to fight.

986
01:45:51,680 --> 01:45:59,000
Praise be to you.
Even if you bleed, you shouldn't fall down.

987
01:45:59,160 --> 01:46:01,920
Thank you father.

988
01:46:18,800 --> 01:46:20,040
﻿Did you finish?

989
01:46:20,040 --> 01:46:23,160
Almost, my Bey.
After counting this chest.

990
01:46:24,240 --> 01:46:30,720
Make no mistakes. Careful brother,
or Bayindir Bey won't stop talking.

991
01:46:30,920 --> 01:46:33,480
﻿May Allah prevent it Bey.

992
01:46:33,920 --> 01:46:38,000
﻿-Alright, let me know when it is finished.
-Thank you Bey.

993
01:46:38,080 --> 01:46:40,040
﻿Come on.

994
01:46:46,440 --> 01:46:56,160
Quickly, take everything away.
Come on don't occupy the courtyard.

995
01:46:58,320 --> 01:47:04,400
When will you take these from here,
horses will go out.

996
01:47:06,600 --> 01:47:11,080
﻿Don't worry, I will take care of it.

997
01:47:13,120 --> 01:47:17,120
﻿Quickly, quickly.

998
01:47:32,360 --> 01:47:35,040
﻿Thank you, Bey.

999
01:47:35,240 --> 01:47:38,800
﻿May Allah bless our Bey.

1000
01:47:40,280 --> 01:47:41,720
﻿Osman Bey.

1001
01:47:57,400 --> 01:48:03,360
-Peace be upon you.
-Peace be upon you too, Yakup Bey.

1002
01:48:03,680 --> 01:48:08,960
﻿Welcome, Osman Bey.

1003
01:48:10,480 --> 01:48:14,300
We are welcomed.
We are welcomed.

1004
01:48:16,240 --> 01:48:22,400
﻿Then, where does this money come from?

1005
01:48:22,480 --> 01:48:32,640
You are giving away your gold.
Was it inheritance or did you do some digging?

1006
01:48:39,000 --> 01:48:46,520
﻿Why do you ask? Are you keeping our gold counted?

1007
01:48:48,200 --> 01:48:54,840
-We claimed a big debt, that is it.
-Okay.

1008
01:48:55,960 --> 01:49:01,960
﻿Your wealth can only make me happy, Osman Bey.

1009
01:49:02,240 --> 01:49:07,960
﻿That is what I thought as well.

1010
01:49:10,000 --> 01:49:20,240
﻿Look here, I want to buy all of these stalls here.

1011
01:49:20,600 --> 01:49:26,600
﻿I thought you would be happy if I had more stalls here.

1012
01:49:26,760 --> 01:49:29,080
﻿-Osman Bey.
-Everyone..

1013
01:49:29,160 --> 01:49:32,720
﻿Has equal rights, Osman Bey.

1014
01:49:32,840 --> 01:49:37,800
﻿-We do not want a single hand in our bazaar.
-The stalls Osman Bey pointed..

1015
01:49:38,200 --> 01:49:46,280
Are equal of yours, Saadet Hatun.
To make it not single hand, it must be made equal.

1016
01:49:46,400 --> 01:49:49,400
Praise be.

1017
01:49:49,640 --> 01:50:01,320
What are you going to do with these stalls?
Do you have goods to sell in that inheritance?

1018
01:50:05,840 --> 01:50:13,240
Come, come here. Here is Ayhan Agha.
We made a deal with him.

1019
01:50:13,440 --> 01:50:18,240
﻿He has brought the biggest caravan this land has ever seen.

1020
01:50:18,480 --> 01:50:27,800
﻿In these stalls, we will sell his goods.

1021
01:50:27,920 --> 01:50:34,120
﻿-Welcome to our bazaar, Ayhan Agha.
-I am welcomed, Yakup Bey.

1022
01:50:34,200 --> 01:50:38,720
Where do you come from?
I've never seen you before.

1023
01:50:39,080 --> 01:50:45,040
There is not much time to visit home, Yakup Bey.
From Damascus to Samarkand..

1024
01:50:45,240 --> 01:50:50,000
﻿And to Indian land to the land of Greek, I set my caravan.

1025
01:50:50,360 --> 01:50:56,600
I will make your bazaar, and our Osman Bey,
very wealthy.

1026
01:50:56,680 --> 01:51:02,760
-If Allah permits.
-If Allah permits.

1027
01:51:03,320 --> 01:51:07,960
If Alalh permits.

1028
01:51:08,320 --> 01:51:10,440
﻿-Bayindir Bey.
-Bey.

1029
01:51:10,640 --> 01:51:15,320
Go to those stalls,
speak with their owners.

1030
01:51:15,440 --> 01:51:19,600
Pay a little more than
what they put to their goods..

1031
01:51:19,920 --> 01:51:24,760
﻿-And buy them all.
-As you command.

1032
01:51:28,520 --> 01:51:37,240
Cerkutay Bey, take care of Bayindir Bey,
so the business is done right.

1033
01:51:37,680 --> 01:51:41,640
﻿As you command, Yakup Bey.

1034
01:51:51,160 --> 01:51:53,560
-Kanyumaz.
-My Bey.

1035
01:51:53,800 --> 01:51:58,320
﻿-Ready the arbour.
-As you command, Bey.

1036
01:51:58,680 --> 01:52:02,120
﻿You are invited, Osman Bey.

1037
01:52:02,520 --> 01:52:06,440
﻿Let us go then.

1038
01:52:20,800 --> 01:52:26,000
﻿Be quick, we can not wait here.

1039
01:52:42,000 --> 01:52:46,840
﻿Tell me, Ayhan Agha.
What business do you do?

1040
01:52:47,080 --> 01:52:52,520
﻿Whatever that land needs, Yakup Bey.

1041
01:52:52,800 --> 01:52:59,040
I load a big caravan.
While the head of the caravan leaves city..

1042
01:52:59,280 --> 01:53:07,120
﻿The back of it must not have left it. However..

1043
01:53:07,480 --> 01:53:13,760
A lot of Alps and soldiers
are needed for protection.

1044
01:53:13,960 --> 01:53:22,800
Issues like these are not a problem
in my land, do not worry.

1045
01:53:23,160 --> 01:53:27,880
﻿I will provide protection.

1046
01:53:31,320 --> 01:53:36,680
﻿Very well.

1047
01:53:37,080 --> 01:53:43,440
﻿Yakup Bey. Sorry to say this.

1048
01:53:43,840 --> 01:53:47,840
However, we will provide
protection for this caravan.

1049
01:53:48,120 --> 01:53:53,760
We already made a deal.
Then why would we buy these stalls?

1050
01:53:54,000 --> 01:53:59,600
﻿Of course. Osman Bey will protect our caravan.

1051
01:54:00,440 --> 01:54:06,440
﻿-Of course they will protect it well.
-Of course we will.

1052
01:54:06,560 --> 01:54:15,280
﻿We always protect those with us, Mehmet Bey.

1053
01:54:27,960 --> 01:54:34,600
﻿Goods have safely arrived Saadet Hatun.
-What is it Saadet Hatun?

1054
01:54:34,680 --> 01:54:39,280
You didn't leave any rugs on frontiers
what are you going to do with them?

1055
01:54:39,520 --> 01:54:42,200
﻿For business.

1056
01:54:42,680 --> 01:54:50,600
You resented much for these rugs.
Take no offence.

1057
01:54:52,840 --> 01:54:59,600
No, just out of curiosity.
Open one and let's see how are they.

1058
01:55:00,240 --> 01:55:04,080
﻿Come on.

1059
01:55:25,880 --> 01:55:32,520
﻿Fitnat! Why are they like this!

1060
01:55:33,960 --> 01:55:37,040
﻿-Alps!
-The rugs were wrapped.

1061
01:55:37,120 --> 01:55:42,120
We never thought of looking inside.
We've just been told to pick them up.

1062
01:55:47,080 --> 01:55:50,480
﻿Open the rest.

1063
01:55:53,080 --> 01:56:00,240
Hatuns will deliver the rugs wrapped
to the alps that will come for pick up.

1064
01:56:00,360 --> 01:56:05,800
They will give the unsold and
left-behind rugs to Saadet Hatun.

1065
01:56:05,880 --> 01:56:12,440
You are very cunning, mother.
She can not use let alone sell those rugs.

1066
01:56:12,680 --> 01:56:20,360
We will make those pay,
who insult the hard work of Kayi Tribe.

1067
01:56:28,760 --> 01:56:30,840
﻿All of them are like this.

1068
01:56:33,720 --> 01:56:36,000
﻿Well, Saadet Hatun..

1069
01:56:36,040 --> 01:56:40,240
It seems you collected all the
flawed rugs in the frontiers.

1070
01:56:40,360 --> 01:56:43,880
Luckily, the news ones showed up
thanks to you.

1071
01:56:47,160 --> 01:56:51,520
Well...
These are no good for trading.

1072
01:56:51,600 --> 01:56:55,200
Why did you buy them?
Didn't you check at all?

1073
01:56:59,320 --> 01:57:05,720
Hatuns, unroll our rugs!
Let people see the fine quality.

1074
01:57:10,120 --> 01:57:12,600
﻿Fools.

1075
01:57:31,720 --> 01:57:36,960
My Bey, as you ordered,
we bought all the stands.

1076
01:57:37,160 --> 01:57:40,320
Thank you, thank you.

1077
01:57:43,760 --> 01:57:48,080
Everything has been handled properly,
Yakup Bey.

1078
01:57:48,600 --> 01:57:50,760
﻿Yet..

1079
01:57:51,400 --> 01:57:54,680
﻿Since the tribe people are privileged,

1080
01:57:54,800 --> 01:57:58,760
...Ayhan Agha's goods
coming from the other lands....

1081
01:57:58,800 --> 01:58:00,960
﻿..will be taxed double.

1082
01:58:06,040 --> 01:58:08,480
﻿No problem.

1083
01:58:10,240 --> 01:58:14,760
﻿Whatever the owner of the market says,

1084
01:58:16,400 --> 01:58:19,360
﻿...we will comply with it.

1085
01:58:21,480 --> 01:58:23,800
﻿That's good.

1086
01:58:24,520 --> 01:58:29,680
﻿Those who want no problems will obey...

1087
01:58:29,720 --> 01:58:33,560
﻿...what the owner says. Both the peace...

1088
01:58:34,440 --> 01:58:38,640
﻿...and unity can only be provided like this.

1089
01:58:42,560 --> 01:58:45,560
﻿Ayhan Agha said well.

1090
01:58:45,640 --> 01:58:48,640
﻿If the decision is made truthfully..

1091
01:58:52,040 --> 01:58:54,320
﻿..then no one will stand against it, Yakup Bey.

1092
01:58:54,400 --> 01:58:58,800
The decision is right.
The one who obeys the right decision...

1093
01:58:58,960 --> 01:59:02,720
﻿...always gets his reward.

1094
01:59:04,120 --> 01:59:08,640
Ayhan Agha.
You proved your commercial morality...

1095
01:59:08,960 --> 01:59:12,480
﻿..by not objecting.

1096
01:59:12,840 --> 01:59:17,640
You will pay the same amount of tax
like everyone else.

1097
01:59:19,920 --> 01:59:25,720
﻿We always reward our companions.

1098
01:59:26,520 --> 01:59:29,360
﻿Yakup Bey...

1099
01:59:30,920 --> 01:59:35,480
Now you are making a decision
because Ayhan Agha...

1100
01:59:36,840 --> 01:59:39,600
﻿...accepted your dominance.

1101
01:59:41,840 --> 01:59:46,840
But this land is not only the
marketplace of frontiers...

1102
01:59:47,520 --> 01:59:51,040
﻿It is not a land of traders who sell their...

1103
01:59:51,160 --> 01:59:54,920
..votes for rewards.

1104
01:59:57,160 --> 02:00:01,920
-See the difference.
-Osman Bey.

1105
02:00:03,200 --> 02:00:07,200
﻿Allah is the Greatest!
Allah is the Greatest!

1106
02:00:07,320 --> 02:00:12,120
-O Allah.
-Allah is..

1107
02:00:12,200 --> 02:00:14,320
﻿Great Allah..

1108
02:00:14,560 --> 02:00:18,040
Great Allah.,
-...the Greatest!

1109
02:00:19,160 --> 02:00:21,240
﻿Anyway.

1110
02:00:21,840 --> 02:00:25,280
Let's not go on and on
about the issue.

1111
02:00:27,360 --> 02:00:34,360
Cerkutay Bey...
Help Ayhan Agha settle in his tent.

1112
02:00:35,320 --> 02:00:40,160
And we will perform salaat with
Osman Bey and then have dinner.

1113
02:00:46,160 --> 02:00:48,440
﻿Let's talk about what..

1114
02:00:48,520 --> 02:00:53,280
﻿...dominance and sultanate are.

1115
02:00:53,560 --> 02:00:56,400
﻿Sure.

1116
02:01:07,480 --> 02:01:11,440
How could you do this?
You bought all the faded...

1117
02:01:11,560 --> 02:01:14,440
﻿..old and damaged carpets!

1118
02:01:14,520 --> 02:01:17,800
﻿Didn't you look at them for once, Fitnat?

1119
02:01:17,880 --> 02:01:20,560
Since we said "buy all the carpets"
to our Alps...

1120
02:01:20,680 --> 02:01:23,880
...they did not check.
They bought all of them.

1121
02:01:24,160 --> 02:01:28,960
-Can I come in, Saadet Hatun?
-Come in.

1122
02:01:31,560 --> 02:01:37,000
What is wrong, Saadet Hatun?
You seem angry.

1123
02:01:37,760 --> 02:01:40,760
﻿Did you lose your money?

1124
02:01:41,640 --> 02:01:47,640
How can these carpets make us lose money?
Who do you think Germiyans are?

1125
02:02:05,360 --> 02:02:11,200
This is the gold for the damaged
carpets you bought. It is all here.

1126
02:02:11,360 --> 02:02:14,160
﻿What are you trying to do?

1127
02:02:14,280 --> 02:02:17,200
﻿We do not sell flawed goods, Saadet Hatun.

1128
02:02:17,400 --> 02:02:20,960
And I know why you
wanted to buy those carpets.

1129
02:02:21,200 --> 02:02:25,280
What does that mean?
Is it a mistake to trade now?

1130
02:02:25,440 --> 02:02:27,280
﻿Trade?

1131
02:02:29,120 --> 02:02:33,360
﻿Anyway. Now you learnt...

1132
02:02:33,560 --> 02:02:40,240
You cannot sell a single thing
without informing me at the frontiers.

1133
02:02:43,600 --> 02:02:49,400
Fitnat! Take this gold and
give it to our people!

1134
02:02:49,480 --> 02:02:53,440
﻿This can only be my charity to the poor!

1135
02:02:58,120 --> 02:03:01,440
﻿I will make you pay for this Malhun.

1136
02:03:02,520 --> 02:03:05,120
﻿I will.

1137
02:03:48,400 --> 02:03:51,960
﻿Come on! This way!

1138
02:03:58,720 --> 02:04:01,720
GERMIYANOGULLARI BORDER

1139
02:04:14,280 --> 02:04:21,960
I organized this dinner and let only
two families attend on purpose.

1140
02:04:22,040 --> 02:04:27,240
﻿I wanted our dinner to be genuine.

1141
02:04:27,880 --> 02:04:32,040
﻿I wanted our friendship to be stronger.

1142
02:04:34,880 --> 02:04:41,240
I wanted the words which couldn't
be said in front of other people...

1143
02:04:41,720 --> 02:04:45,120
﻿..to be said around this table.

1144
02:04:45,920 --> 02:04:49,520
Why would the ones who are always
honest and blunt in a crowd...

1145
02:04:50,520 --> 02:04:53,960
﻿...need to be alone to say their words?

1146
02:04:59,200 --> 02:05:02,000
Fair enough.

1147
02:05:09,880 --> 02:05:13,600
﻿May what you eat and drink be yours.

1148
02:05:13,680 --> 02:05:17,960
Now I will talk about our actual issue.

1149
02:05:18,040 --> 02:05:23,320
﻿Sure we will. Let's talk about conquests.

1150
02:05:23,440 --> 02:05:27,000
﻿We took Lefke for a reason.

1151
02:05:27,200 --> 02:05:30,440
﻿Not conquests, Osman Bey...

1152
02:05:30,800 --> 02:05:37,200
﻿We will talk about conquests after you pledge allegiance.

1153
02:05:42,640 --> 02:05:48,560
I proved that my only intention
was conquering lands...

1154
02:05:48,720 --> 02:05:51,760
﻿...with the conquest of Lefke.

1155
02:05:52,000 --> 02:05:55,960
﻿I also proved that my intention was being a union...

1156
02:05:56,080 --> 02:06:01,040
﻿...by giving Lefke to you. Now you..

1157
02:06:01,360 --> 02:06:07,400
...can prove that fighting for Islam,
conquests and union are your goals.

1158
02:06:15,120 --> 02:06:18,000
﻿We all know each other.

1159
02:06:18,360 --> 02:06:23,160
﻿-Announce your obedience, Osman Bey.
-Yakup Bey.

1160
02:06:24,080 --> 02:06:27,840
﻿Yakup Bey.

1161
02:06:29,080 --> 02:06:34,680
Taking the castle before methat
I was already acting on..

1162
02:06:35,200 --> 02:06:38,400
﻿Doesn't prove anything.

1163
02:06:43,920 --> 02:06:49,160
None of these things you said,
are a reason to obey.

1164
02:07:19,120 --> 02:07:25,720
They are in the treasure room.
Get ready, quickly.

1165
02:07:32,120 --> 02:07:36,520
﻿Who are you?

1166
02:08:47,920 --> 02:08:51,040
﻿Atmaca, someone's coming.

1167
02:09:08,440 --> 02:09:10,680
﻿Quickly.

1168
02:09:11,360 --> 02:09:14,280
﻿Quickly, faster.

1169
02:09:26,160 --> 02:09:31,160
﻿Orhan Bey. There you are.

1170
02:09:36,800 --> 02:09:39,640
﻿Alps! Some got in!

1171
02:10:05,480 --> 02:10:09,120
﻿You go and help them get the treasure.

1172
02:10:19,640 --> 02:10:25,400
Your mask won't save you, devil.
Come here! Come!

1173
02:11:26,640 --> 02:11:29,000
﻿-Bey!
-The treasure.

1174
02:11:29,080 --> 02:11:32,160
﻿-Bey!
-Treasure.

1175
02:11:32,400 --> 02:11:35,640
﻿Bey! Orhan Bey!

1176
02:11:36,200 --> 02:11:39,800
﻿Bey! Hold on Bey!

1177
02:11:46,640 --> 02:11:49,440
﻿Atmaca, Vasilis is coming.

1178
02:11:53,480 --> 02:11:57,440
Alps are coming.
Get out from the barn quickly.

1179
02:11:57,560 --> 02:12:01,040
﻿Follow me.

1180
02:12:23,640 --> 02:12:28,600
﻿Alps!

1181
02:12:39,720 --> 02:12:43,520
﻿I killed their leader.

1182
02:12:44,400 --> 02:12:47,320
I couldn't catch their leader,
they ran away.

1183
02:12:47,800 --> 02:12:50,600
﻿They went towards the kitchen.

1184
02:12:52,000 --> 02:12:55,480
﻿You go after them.

1185
02:13:13,320 --> 02:13:18,360
There is no unity like this.
You create a duality.

1186
02:13:18,520 --> 02:13:21,600
﻿This is no time to create duality.

1187
02:13:21,680 --> 02:13:25,040
﻿Why am I the one causing conflict?

1188
02:13:25,360 --> 02:13:27,280
﻿Tell me.

1189
02:13:28,800 --> 02:13:32,120
﻿Did I tell you do not be the Sultan

1190
02:13:32,520 --> 02:13:35,040
﻿Your banner is different.

1191
02:13:35,960 --> 02:13:38,600
﻿And mine is different.

1192
02:13:38,720 --> 02:13:42,640
Having two heads is the same as
having no head at all.

1193
02:13:42,720 --> 02:13:45,960
﻿It's not right, Osman Bey. It is not!

1194
02:13:46,120 --> 02:13:48,600
﻿What are you worried about?

1195
02:13:49,280 --> 02:13:53,760
Tell me Yakup Bey.
What are you worried about?

1196
02:13:58,920 --> 02:14:04,200
are you afraid that all of the
Beys will gather behind me?

1197
02:14:06,960 --> 02:14:11,600
﻿Stop there. Stop it.

1198
02:14:12,600 --> 02:14:18,120
The pledge you are talking about is not
for the sake of holy case.

1199
02:14:19,920 --> 02:14:23,040
﻿It is for the sake of suppressing your rival.

1200
02:14:23,840 --> 02:14:28,640
﻿-Osman Bey!
-Stop.

1201
02:14:44,160 --> 02:14:49,880
Are you equal to me
that you can be my rival?

1202
02:14:51,520 --> 02:14:59,240
I see you as my brother,
having the same blood as you.

1203
02:15:03,000 --> 02:15:10,000
It might result in a disaster
if you do not pledge loyalty to me.

1204
02:15:10,080 --> 02:15:15,360
﻿Evil ones may cause conflict. No.

1205
02:15:17,040 --> 02:15:21,080
﻿I will not let you do that to our country.

1206
02:15:24,160 --> 02:15:27,720
﻿Now I will ask one last time.

1207
02:15:28,920 --> 02:15:34,400
﻿Are you with me or are you against me?

1208
02:15:59,240 --> 02:16:02,280
﻿Yakup Bey.

1209
02:16:09,640 --> 02:16:15,920
The one who stays in the
shadow has no shadow.

1210
02:16:18,720 --> 02:16:24,440
dreamed about that plane tree that
will be the shadow of many oppressed ones.

1211
02:16:25,480 --> 02:16:30,120
﻿And now you want me to forget about my dream.

1212
02:16:34,879 --> 02:16:38,680
Inform the healers!
No one will leave the palace...

1213
02:16:38,840 --> 02:16:44,000
-...until we find those men!
-I bear witness that none worthy of worship except Allah

1214
02:16:46,040 --> 02:16:52,480
and I bear witness that Muhammad (PBUH)
is His servant and Messenger.

1215
02:16:52,559 --> 02:16:58,600
﻿My Bey! Hang on my Bey!

1216
02:17:01,719 --> 02:17:07,920
﻿But I see that you are after the same dream.

1217
02:17:11,799 --> 02:17:14,799
﻿You didn't leave us in a tight spot.

1218
02:17:16,480 --> 02:17:19,879
﻿You gave us the castle you took by fighting.

1219
02:17:21,120 --> 02:17:23,360
﻿Even more,

1220
02:17:25,520 --> 02:17:28,080
﻿you protected my brave boy.

1221
02:17:32,879 --> 02:17:36,680
﻿I know that your intentions are well.

1222
02:17:39,200 --> 02:17:43,360
If we do not stray away from
the path of Allah's words...

1223
02:17:44,840 --> 02:17:48,559
﻿I'll be behind you from now on.

1224
02:17:57,120 --> 02:18:02,719
﻿Then pledge your loyalty Osman Bey.

1225
02:18:11,160 --> 02:18:14,080
﻿From now on,

1226
02:18:18,639 --> 02:18:24,799
﻿Kayis will obey Germiyanoglus.

1227
02:18:48,840 --> 02:18:54,840
﻿Since you pledged loyalty and we have united,

1228
02:18:55,000 --> 02:19:01,240
﻿let all the conflicts end. Come on.

1229
02:19:19,959 --> 02:19:26,559
﻿Come on, come here. Come on.

1230
02:19:34,360 --> 02:19:37,240
﻿Come on.

1231
02:20:29,040 --> 02:20:31,840
﻿We will be behind
you from now on.

1232
02:20:37,800 --> 02:20:41,440
﻿It will be a new beginning for all of us.